\\ redacted for the release: paths of the development workspace, which is not shipped
\\ richelot.gp: descent by a Richelot isogeny for Jacobians of genus 2 curves over a number field (PARI/GP 2.17).
\\
\\ SETTING. K = Q[v]/(Kpol) (any variable v other than x; K = Q is Kpol = y), d in K not a square, L = K(sqrt d),
\\ tau the generator of Gal(L/K). The curve is
\\     F : y^2 = f(x) = c * G1(x) * G2(x) * G3(x),   G2 = A + sqrt(d) B,  G3 = tau(G2) = A - sqrt(d) B,
\\ with c in K, G1, A, B in K[x], deg G1 in {1, 2}, max(deg A, deg B) = 2 (so f has degree 6, or 5 when deg G1 = 1).
\\ Delta = {0, T0, T1, T2}, T0 = [roots of G1], T1 = [roots of G2], T2 = [roots of G3] (class of the difference of the
\\ two roots), is a K-rational maximal isotropic subgroup of J[2] with Delta ~ F2[Gal(L/K)] as a Galois module, so
\\ H^1(K, Delta) = L^x / L^x2 (Shapiro), and likewise for the dual kernel Delta'.
\\
\\ RICHELOT DUAL (Cassels-Flynn, Prolegomena, ch. 9; twist fixed by Bruin-Doerksen, arXiv 0902.3480, Section
\\ "Richelot isogenies", Proposition T:twist, whose determinant has rows G_i and columns the coefficients of 1, x, x^2).
\\ With H1 = G2'G3 - G2G3', H2 = G3'G1 - G3G1', H3 = G1'G2 - G1G2', Det = det[g_ij] (row i = coefficients of x^0, x^1,
\\ x^2 of G_i, without c), the codomain J' = J/Delta is the Jacobian of F' : Det y^2 = c H1 H2 H3. In terms of A, B:
\\ H1 = 2 s (A B' - A' B), H2 = P - s Q, H3 = -tau(H2), Det = -2 s D0, with s = sqrt d, P = A' G1 - A G1',
\\ Q = B' G1 - B G1', D0 = det(g1; a; b). Hence F' has the same shape:
\\     F' : y^2 = (c / D0) * R(x) * (P^2 - d Q^2),  G1' = R = A B' - A' B,  A' = P,  B' = -Q  (G2' = H2).
\\ The K-rational Richelot correspondence (BD's Gamma_d for the pair G2, G3)
\\ is G1(x) R(z) = D0 (x - z)^2, y y' = c (x - z) G2(x) H2(z).
\\
\\ KUMMER MAPS. kappa : J(K) -> H^1(K, Delta') = L^x/L^x2, [E - Dinf] -> G2(E) (E effective of degree 2, rational
\\ over K, Dinf = the divisor above x = infinity), is the connecting map of phi^ : J' -> J, kernel phi^(J'(K)); the same
\\ formula on F' (with H2) gives J'(K) -> H^1(K, Delta) with kernel phi(J(K)). G2 has divisor 2 (W3 + W4 - Dinf), a
\\ representative of T1 in Delta = ker phi; at a root of G2 the function c G1 G3 (= G2 times a square) is used, at
\\ infinity G2 / x^2 (value lc(G2)); these mixed evaluations are well defined by Weil reciprocity (tame symbols).
\\ Formula used: kappa(E) = Res(u1, G2) * Res(g, c G1 G3) * lc(G2)^(deg u) with u the monic x-polynomial of E,
\\ g = gcd(u, G2), u1 = u / g; for odd deg u, E is completed by the rational point at infinity.
\\
\\ LOCAL IMAGES. Every class of J(K_v) is [E - Dinf] with E an effective K_v-rational divisor of degree 2 (genus 2),
\\ so Im_v(kappa) is generated by the values at pairs of K_v-points and at pairs of conjugate points over the
\\ quadratic extensions K_v(sqrt e). At a finite place v the points are produced, in this order, by
\\  (1) a tree of residue discs in P^1(K_v) (rich_ratpoints): discs on which the square classes of f and G2 are
\\      constant (sufficient Taylor test: ratio to the centre value in 1 + 4 pi O) give one point, discs free of zeros
\\      but not yet constant (only above 2) give a few random points, other discs are refined (depth and node caps);
\\  (2) the same tree in (al, be) for x = al + be sqrt(e), in each field K_v(sqrt e), e over the nontrivial classes of
\\      K_v^x / squares (at most 63 of them, chosen at random when there are more) (rich_quadpoints);
\\  (3) random rational and quadratic points (x = pi^k r, k from a mixture concentrated near 0) until the count.
\\ At a real place only (3) is used. At a finite place of degree one above p <= 3 (where the global trees stall on
\\ deep ramification) the search runs on a local model of K_v instead (section "local model" below): a root finder
\\ for f - y0^2 over K_v and its quadratic extensions (Newton polygon scaling, residue disc tree, Newton iteration,
\\ deflation), y-sampling from fresh and nearby starts, and a 2-adic approximate square root; every point it
\\ returns is a global point of K or K(sqrt e) and is checked globally before its Kummer value enters a basis.
\\ Local Tate duality: the two images are exact annihilators of each other, so
\\ dim Im_v(kappa) + dim Im_v(kappa') = dim H^1(K_v, Delta) = sum over w | v of dim L_w^x / L_w^x2
\\ ([L_w : Q_2] + 2 above 2, 2 at odd w, 1 at real w when L_v = R x R, 0 at complex places). The search stops exactly
\\ when this count is reached; the two found subspaces are then the full images (each lies in its image and the
\\ dimensions add up). Every recorded value is the kappa value of a genuine K_v-rational divisor, so going over the
\\ count raises an error (it would contradict duality); not reaching it within the budget raises an error (unless
\\ rich_partial_ok = 1: see PARTIAL IMAGES AND BOUNDS). No step
\\ of the search needs to be exhaustive: only the final count certifies the local images.
\\
\\ SQUARE CLASSES. At a prime w of L: coordinates (v_w(a) mod 2, ideallog of a / pi^v_w(a) in (O/w^k)^x / squares)
\\ with k = 2 e_w + 1 above 2 (1 + w^(2e+1) consists of squares) and k = 1 at odd w (idealstar with cycmod = 2).
\\ At a real place: the sign bits. Checked against nfislocalpower in richelot_test.gp.
\\
\\ SELMER GROUPS. S = places of K above 2, above the given bad primes, where L/K ramifies, and the real places where
\\ L_v = R x R. L(S, 2) = O_{S u A}^x / squares with A a set of auxiliary primes whose classes form a basis of
\\ Cl_S(L) / 2 (then Cl_{S u A}(L) has odd order and every S u A-unit has even valuation at A, which is checked).
\\ bnfinit / bnfunits are conditional on GRH unless the field data are certified (bnfcertify); the output records it.
\\ Sel^phihat = {a in L(S,2) : res_v(a) in Im_v(kappa) for v in S} (J side, contains J(K)/phi^ J'(K)),
\\ Sel^phi = same with kappa' (J' side, contains J'(K)/phi J(K)).
\\ RANK. dim J(K)/2J(K) = dim J'(K)/phi J(K) + dim J(K)/phi^ J'(K) - dim(J'(K)[phi^] / phi(J(K)[2])), and here
\\ Delta(K) = {0, T0}, Delta'(K) = {0, T0'}, so the last term is 2 - dim J(K)[2] and
\\     rank J(K) = dim J'(K)/phi J(K) + dim J(K)/phi^ J'(K) - 2 <= dim Sel^phi + dim Sel^phihat - 2.
\\
\\ PARTIAL IMAGES AND BOUNDS. With rich_partial_ok = 1, rich_localimages returns the bases found so far (7th entry 0)
\\ after maxtries rounds or rich_time_budget ms, and rich_selmer_bounds turns possibly partial images into bounds:
\\ lower: the subgroup of L(S,2) localizing into the spans of the found bases (inside the Selmer group);
\\ upper: localizations orthogonal to the found basis of the other side for the Tate pairing, which is
\\ sum_{w | v} (a, tau b)_w (the plain pairing sum_w (a, b)_w and this one are the only Galois invariant perfect pairings
\\ on F2[Gal(L/K)]; the complete places decide between them, and the test suite finds the tau pairing everywhere);
\\ both refined by the Greenberg-Wiles (Cassels) formula
\\     dim Sel^phihat - dim Sel^phi = sum_v (dim Im_v(kappa) - dim Delta'(K_v)) - 2 r2(K) - #(real places not split in L),
\\ the sum over the places of S, with Im_v(kappa) between the found dimension and N_v minus the found dimension on
\\ the other side (this part needs neither GRH nor the pairing identification).
\\
\\ INTERFACE (x is the polynomial variable; L elements are t_POLMOD in the variable zL; Maps are accessed by mapget)
\\   F  = rich_fields(Kpol, d, {wantbnf = 1})         field data (nfK, L, sqrt d, tau, real places, bnf of L);
\\                                                      wantbnf may be a precomputed bnf of L (same polredbest polynomial)
\\   R  = rich_curve(F, c, G1, A, B)                    curve data (f, D0, G2, G3 over L, ...)
\\   Rd = rich_dual(F, R)                               Richelot dual F' in the same format
\\   rich_kappa(F, R, u)                                Kummer value in L^x of the divisor with x-polynomial u
\\   rich_place(F, v)                                   local data at v (prime ideal of K, or index of a real place)
\\   rich_loccoord(F, P, a)                             F2 coordinates of a in L_v^x / squares (a in L^x or famat)
\\   rich_loccoords(F, P, gens)                         the same for a list (matrix of columns, famat bases cached)
\\   rich_sqinit(nf, pr), rich_sqcoord(nf, S, a)        square class coordinates at one prime of any number field
\\   rich_ratpoints(F, R, P, {maxdepth}, {maxnodes = 4000}, {nsamp = 8})     candidate points of R(K_v) (disc tree)
\\   rich_quadpoints(F, R, P, Q, {maxdepth}, {maxnodes = 3000}, {nsamp = 8}) kappa values of quadratic points over
\\                                                      Q = rich_quadfield(F, P, e) (polydisc tree)
\\   rich_localimages(F, R, Rd, P, {maxtries = 20000})  [basis Im_v(kappa), basis Im_v(kappa'), dim H^1, values,
\\                                                      random rounds used, dimension found by the trees, complete]
\\   rich_gram(F, P)                                    [G1, G0]: Gram matrices of sum_w (a, tau b)_w and sum_w (a, b)_w
\\   rich_places(F, R, badp)                            the set S (Maps from rich_place)
\\   rich_LS2(F, SL)                                    [generators of L(S,2) as famat, auxiliary primes]
\\   rich_selmer(F, R, Rd, badp, {verbose = 0})         Map: "s" (dim Sel^phi), "shat" (dim Sel^phihat), "bound",
\\                                                      "t2", "t2d", "LS2dim", "local", "grh", "selhat", "sel", ...
\\   rich_selmer_bounds(F, R, Rd, pl, loc, {gramN = oo})  Map: "low", "up" (bounds for [dim Sel^phihat, dim Sel^phi]),
\\                                                      "cassels", "tw", "T0", "LS2dim", "locrank", "places", ...
\\                                                      from possibly partial images loc[k] at the places pl[k]
\\   rich_tors2(F, R)                                   dim J(K)[2] from the quadratic factors of f over K
\\   rich_locsolv(nf, pr, f, {maxdepth = 40}, {maxnodes = 20000})   y^2 = f(x) over K_pr: [1, witness] (point),
\\                                                      [0] (no point, proved by the disc tree) or [-1] (undecided)
\\   rich_reduce(F, R, pr)                              [p, d, c, G1, A, B] reduced modulo a degree one prime of K
\\ ASSUMPTIONS. d is not a square in K; D0 != 0 (else J/Delta is a product of elliptic curves: not handled);
\\ f squarefree; the bad primes passed to rich_selmer contain every prime of bad reduction of J (primes dividing
\\ 2 * disc * denominators are always safe; rich_badprimes gives such a list).
\\ GLOBALS. rich_verbose, rich_partial_ok, rich_time_budget, rich_lv_qtrees (below).
\\ The caller sets default(parisizemax) (not done here: that default inside a read() file skips the rest).

zL; zM;
rich_qa = varhigher("rich_qa"); rich_qb = varhigher("rich_qb"); rich_lastnodes = 0;
rich_verbose = 0;  \\ 1: progress of rich_localimages (fields, dimensions, times)
rich_partial_ok = 0;  \\ 1: rich_localimages returns the partial bases (7th entry 0) instead of an error after maxtries rounds
rich_time_budget = 0;  \\ with rich_partial_ok = 1: stop the random rounds of rich_localimages after this many ms (0: no limit)
rich_lv_qtrees = 2;  \\ number of quadratic fields searched by the polydisc trees at the local model places

rich_chk(c, msg) = if (!c, error("richelot: ", msg));

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- elements and polynomials
rich_xcoefs(P) = if (type(P) == "t_POL" && variable(P) == 'x, Vec(P), [P]);

\\ normalise an element of K (t_INT, t_FRAC, polynomial in v, t_POLMOD mod Kpol)
rich_Kelt(F, a) =
{
  my(Kpol = mapget(F, "Kpol"), v = variable(Kpol));
  if (type(a) == "t_POLMOD", a = lift(a));
  if (poldegree(Kpol) == 1, return(subst(a, v, -polcoef(Kpol, 0) / polcoef(Kpol, 1))));
  Mod(a, Kpol);
}

\\ Helpers replacing closures: a closure that captures a large object (F, LV, nf, bnf) and is stored in a local
\\ variable leaks a copy of that object on the heap at every call (PARI/GP 2.17.4, measured), hence named functions.
rich_rndK(nfK, n, p) = if (n == 1, random(p^10), nfbasistoalg(nfK, vectorv(n, i, random(p^10))));
rich_rp_pt(F, pi, sd, a, m, t) = my(z = rich_Kelt(F, a + pi^m * t)); if (sd == 1, z, if (z == 0, [], 1 / z));
rich_toMx(F, Q, h) = Pol(apply(cc -> rich_KtoM(F, Q, cc), Vec(h)), 'x);
rich_lv_vfv(LV, Qd, z) = if (Qd == 0, [rich_lv_val(LV, z)], rich_lv_qvals(LV, Qd, z));
rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, z) = if (Qd == 0, rich_lv_val(LV, z), rich_lv_qvals(LV, Qd, z)[1]);
rich_lv_rp_pt(LV, I, sd, a) = my(z = rich_lv_lift(LV, a, I)); if (sd == 1, z, if (z == 0, [], 1 / z));
rich_lv_res(LV, c) =
{
  my(cc = polcoef(lift(Mod(rich_lv_unwrap(c), mapget(LV, "E"))), 0, rich_lY));
  if (type(cc) == "t_PADIC", cc = truncate(cc));
  lift(Mod(cc, mapget(LV, "p")));
}
rich_hpair(nfL, P, a, b) =
{
  if (mapget(P, "type") == 0,
    my(js = mapget(P, "js")); sum(k = 1, #js, nfeltsign(nfL, a, js[k]) < 0 && nfeltsign(nfL, b, js[k]) < 0) % 2
  ,
    my(W = mapget(P, "W")); sum(k = 1, #W, nfhilbert(nfL, a, b, W[k]) < 0) % 2);
}
rich_redp(F, nfK, p, mp, a) =
{
  if (mp == 0, return(lift(Mod(a, p))));
  my(r = nfmodpr(nfK, lift(rich_Kelt(F, a)), mp)); if (type(r) == "t_FFELT", r = r.pol);
  lift(Mod(polcoef(r, 0), p));
}

rich_Kx(F, P) = Pol(apply(c -> rich_Kelt(F, c), rich_xcoefs(P)), 'x);

rich_KtoL(F, a) =
{
  my(v = variable(mapget(F, "Kpol")), b = rich_Kelt(F, a));
  if (type(b) == "t_POLMOD", b = lift(b));
  subst(b, v, mapget(F, "aL"));
}

rich_isL(c) = type(c) == "t_POLMOD" && variable(c.mod) == 'zL;

rich_toLx(F, P) =
{
  my(V = rich_xcoefs(P));
  if (#[c | c <- V, rich_isL(c)] > 0, return(Pol(V, 'x)));
  Pol(apply(c -> rich_KtoL(F, c), V), 'x);
}

rich_tau(F, a) = if (type(a) == "t_POLMOD", subst(lift(a), 'zL, mapget(F, "tauz")), a);

rich_taux(F, P) = Pol(apply(c -> rich_tau(F, c), rich_xcoefs(P)), 'x);

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- F2 linear algebra
\\ add v to the list B of independent columns (mod 2); returns [B', 1] if the rank increased, else [B, 0]
rich_f2add(B, v) =
{
  my(w = v % 2);
  if (w == 0, return([B, 0]));
  if (#B == 0, return([[w], 1]));
  if (matrank(Mod(Mat(concat(B, [w])), 2)) > #B, [concat(B, [w]), 1], [B, 0]);
}

\\ rows whose common kernel is the span of the columns B inside F2^N
rich_annih(B, N) =
{
  my(K);
  if (#B == 0, return(matid(N)));
  K = matker(Mod(Mat(B)~, 2));
  if (#K == 0, return(matrix(0, N)));
  lift(K)~;
}

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- fields
rich_fields(Kpol, d, wantbnf = 1) =
{
  my(F = Map(), v = variable(Kpol), nfK, dK, eq, L0, a0, k, red, Lpol, Mth, aL, sL, rev, tauz, nfL, bnfL = 0,
     real = List(), r1K, r1L, prec = 100, rts, cand);
  rich_chk(v != 'x, "the variable of Kpol must not be x");
  mapput(F, "Kpol", Kpol);
  nfK = nfinit(Kpol); mapput(F, "nfK", nfK);
  dK = rich_Kelt(F, d); mapput(F, "d", dK);
  rich_chk(dK != 0, "d = 0");
  if (poldegree(Kpol) == 1, rich_chk(!issquare(dK), "d is a square in K"),
                            rich_chk(#nfroots(nfK, x^2 - lift(dK)) == 0, "d is a square in K"));
  eq = rnfequation(nfK, x^2 - if (type(dK) == "t_POLMOD", lift(dK), dK), 1);
  L0 = eq[1]; a0 = lift(eq[2]); k = eq[3];
  red = polredbest(L0, 1);
  Lpol = subst(red[1], 'x, 'zL);
  Mth = Mod(subst(lift(red[2]), 'x, 'zL), Lpol);
  aL = subst(a0, 'x, Mth);
  sL = Mth - k * aL;
  rev = lift(modreverse(red[2]));
  tauz = subst(rev, 'x, 2 * k * aL - Mth);
  mapput(F, "Lpol", Lpol); mapput(F, "aL", aL); mapput(F, "sL", sL); mapput(F, "tauz", tauz);
  rich_chk(sL^2 == rich_KtoL(F, dK), "sqrt(d) in L");
  rich_chk(subst(lift(tauz), 'zL, tauz) == Mod('zL, Lpol), "tau is an involution");
  rich_chk(rich_tau(F, sL) == -sL, "tau(sqrt d) = -sqrt d");
  rich_chk(rich_tau(F, aL) == aL, "tau fixes K");
  \\ a precomputed bnf of L may be passed as wantbnf: it must be for the same polynomial (polredbest of the
  \\ rnfequation polynomial, any variable); its variable is changed to zL by subst
  if (type(wantbnf) == "t_VEC",
    bnfL = subst(wantbnf, variable(wantbnf.pol), 'zL);
    rich_chk(bnfL.pol == Lpol, "the precomputed bnf is not for the polredbest polynomial of L");
    nfL = bnfL.nf
  , if (wantbnf, bnfL = bnfinit(Lpol); nfL = bnfL.nf, nfL = nfinit(Lpol)));
  mapput(F, "nfL", nfL); mapput(F, "bnfL", bnfL);
  \\ real places of K where L_v = R x R: the two real embeddings of L above them (indices in nfL.roots)
  r1K = nfK.sign[1]; r1L = nfL.sign[1];
  for (i = 1, r1K,
    if (nfeltsign(nfK, dK, i) > 0,
      cand = [j | j <- [1..r1L], abs(subst(lift(aL * Mod(1, Lpol)), 'zL, nfL.roots[j]) - nfK.roots[i]) < 10^(-20)];
      rich_chk(#cand == 2, "real embeddings of L above a real place of K");
      listput(real, [i, cand])));
  mapput(F, "real", Vec(real));
  F;
}

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- curves
rich_curve(F, c, G1, A, B) =
{
  my(R = Map(), d = mapget(F, "d"), f, M, D0, sL = mapget(F, "sL"), AL, BL, G1L, G2L, G3L, cL);
  c = rich_Kelt(F, c); G1 = rich_Kx(F, G1); A = rich_Kx(F, A); B = rich_Kx(F, B);
  rich_chk(c != 0, "c = 0");
  rich_chk(poldegree(G1, 'x) == 1 || poldegree(G1, 'x) == 2, "deg G1 must be 1 or 2");
  rich_chk(max(poldegree(A, 'x), poldegree(B, 'x)) == 2, "G2 = A + sqrt(d) B must have degree 2");
  f = c * G1 * (A^2 - d * B^2);
  rich_chk(poldegree(f, 'x) == 5 || poldegree(f, 'x) == 6, "deg f must be 5 or 6");
  rich_chk(poldisc(f) != 0, "f is not squarefree");
  M = matrix(3, 3, i, j, polcoef([G1, A, B][i], j - 1, 'x));
  D0 = matdet(M);
  rich_chk(D0 != 0, "singular quadratic splitting (D0 = 0): J/Delta is a product of elliptic curves");
  AL = rich_toLx(F, A); BL = rich_toLx(F, B); G1L = rich_toLx(F, G1); cL = rich_KtoL(F, c);
  G2L = AL + sL * BL; G3L = AL - sL * BL;
  mapput(R, "c", c); mapput(R, "G1", G1); mapput(R, "A", A); mapput(R, "B", B); mapput(R, "f", f);
  mapput(R, "D0", D0); mapput(R, "G1L", G1L); mapput(R, "G2L", G2L); mapput(R, "G3L", G3L);
  mapput(R, "W2L", cL * G1L * G3L); mapput(R, "lcG2", polcoef(G2L, 2, 'x));
  R;
}

rich_dual(F, R) =
{
  my(G1 = mapget(R, "G1"), A = mapget(R, "A"), B = mapget(R, "B"), c = mapget(R, "c"), D0 = mapget(R, "D0"), P, Q, Rr);
  P = deriv(A, 'x) * G1 - A * deriv(G1, 'x);
  Q = deriv(B, 'x) * G1 - B * deriv(G1, 'x);
  Rr = A * deriv(B, 'x) - deriv(A, 'x) * B;
  rich_curve(F, c / D0, Rr, P, -Q);
}

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- Kummer map (global)
rich_kappa(F, R, u) =
{
  my(uL = rich_toLx(F, u), G2L = mapget(R, "G2L"), g, u1, val);
  rich_chk(uL != 0, "kappa of the zero polynomial");
  uL = uL / pollead(uL);
  g = gcd(uL, G2L); g = g / pollead(g);
  u1 = uL \ g;
  rich_chk(u1 * g == uL, "kappa: division");
  val = polresultant(u1, G2L, 'x);
  if (poldegree(g, 'x) > 0, val *= polresultant(g, mapget(R, "W2L"), 'x));
  if (poldegree(uL, 'x) % 2, val *= mapget(R, "lcG2"));
  rich_chk(val != 0, "kappa: zero value");
  val;
}

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- square classes
rich_sqinit(nf, pr) =
{
  my(p = pr.p, e = pr.e, f = pr.f, bid, ev, want, pi);
  bid = idealstar(nf, idealpow(nf, pr, if (p == 2, 2 * e + 1, 1)), 1, 2);
  ev = [i | i <- [1..#bid.cyc], bid.cyc[i] % 2 == 0];
  want = if (p == 2, e * f + 1, 1);
  rich_chk(#ev == want, Str("dimension of O_w^x / squares: ", #ev, " instead of ", want));
  pi = if (e == 1, p, nfbasistoalg(nf, pr.gen[2]));
  rich_chk(nfeltval(nf, pi, pr) == 1, "uniformizer");
  [pr, pi, bid, ev];
}

rich_alg(nf, a) = if (type(a) == "t_COL", nfbasistoalg(nf, a), a);

rich_sqcoord(nf, S, a) =
{
  my(v, u, lg);
  if (type(a) == "t_MAT",
    if (#a~ == 0, return(vectorv(1 + #S[4])));
    return(sum(i = 1, #a~, a[i, 2] * rich_sqcoord(nf, S, a[i, 1])) % 2));
  a = rich_alg(nf, a);
  v = nfeltval(nf, a, S[1]); u = a / S[2]^v; lg = ideallog(nf, u, S[3]);
  concat([v % 2], vector(#S[4], i, lg[S[4][i]] % 2))~;
}

rich_signcoord(nf, js, a) =
{
  if (type(a) == "t_MAT",
    if (#a~ == 0, return(vectorv(#js)));
    return(sum(i = 1, #a~, a[i, 2] * rich_signcoord(nf, js, a[i, 1])) % 2));
  a = rich_alg(nf, a);
  vector(#js, i, if (nfeltsign(nf, a, js[i]) < 0, 1, 0))~;
}

\\ primes of the field nfb above the prime pr of K; img maps elements of K into nfb
rich_above(nfK, nfb, img, pr) =
{
  my(g = rich_alg(nfK, pr.gen[2]), I = idealadd(nfb, pr.p, img(g)));
  [W | W <- idealprimedec(nfb, pr.p), idealval(nfb, I, W) > 0];
}

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- places
rich_place(F, v) =
{
  my(P = Map(), nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), nfL = mapget(F, "nfL"), js = [], W, sq, N);
  if (type(v) == "t_INT",
    foreach (mapget(F, "real"), r, if (r[1] == v, js = r[2]));
    mapput(P, "type", 0); mapput(P, "i", v); mapput(P, "js", js); mapput(P, "N", #js);
    mapput(P, "name", Str("real ", v));
  ,
    W = rich_above(nfK, nfL, a -> rich_KtoL(F, a), v);
    rich_chk(sum(i = 1, #W, W[i].e * W[i].f) == 2 * v.e * v.f, "primes of L above v");
    sq = [rich_sqinit(nfL, w) | w <- W];
    N = sum(i = 1, #sq, 1 + #sq[i][4]);
    mapput(P, "type", 1); mapput(P, "pr", v); mapput(P, "p", v.p); mapput(P, "W", W); mapput(P, "sq", sq);
    mapput(P, "N", N);
    mapput(P, "piK", rich_Kelt(F, if (v.e == 1, v.p, rich_alg(nfK, v.gen[2]))));
    mapput(P, "name", Str("p = ", v.p, " (e = ", v.e, ", f = ", v.f, "; ", #W, " prime(s) of L)")));
  P;
}

rich_loccoord(F, P, a) =
{
  my(nfL = mapget(F, "nfL"), sq);
  if (mapget(P, "type") == 0, return(rich_signcoord(nfL, mapget(P, "js"), a)));
  sq = mapget(P, "sq");
  concat(vector(#sq, i, rich_sqcoord(nfL, sq[i], a)));
}

\\ coordinate matrix (one column per element) at P of a list of elements or famats; each distinct base element of the
\\ famats is evaluated once (S-unit generators share their base elements), odd exponents only
rich_loccoords(F, P, gens) =
{
  my(cache = Map(), cv, col, g, N = mapget(P, "N"));
  if (#gens == 0, return(matrix(N, 0)));
  Mat(vector(#gens, j,
    g = gens[j]; if (type(g) != "t_MAT", g = Mat([g, 1]));
    col = vectorv(N);
    for (i = 1, #g~, if (g[i, 2] % 2,
      if (!mapisdefined(cache, g[i, 1], &cv), cv = rich_loccoord(F, P, g[i, 1]); mapput(cache, g[i, 1], cv));
      col += cv));
    col % 2));
}


\\ nonzero square at the prime pr of nf. The denominator is cleared by a square first: PARI 2.17.4 nfislocalpower
\\ raises "incorrect type in zk_to_ff" on some elements with p^2 in the denominator.
rich_nfsq(nf, pr, a) =
{
  my(b = rich_alg(nf, a), dn);
  if (b == 0, return(0));
  dn = denominator(content(lift(b)));
  nfislocalpower(nf, pr, b * dn^2, 2);
}

\\ is the local element a (in K) a nonzero square at the place P
rich_locsq(F, P, a) =
{
  if (a == 0, return(0));
  if (mapget(P, "type") == 0, return(nfeltsign(mapget(F, "nfK"), a, mapget(P, "i")) > 0));
  rich_nfsq(mapget(F, "nfK"), mapget(P, "pr"), a);
}

\\ are the points at infinity of the curve rational over K_v
rich_infrat(F, R, P) =
{
  my(f = mapget(R, "f"));
  if (poldegree(f, 'x) == 5, return(1));
  rich_locsq(F, P, pollead(f));
}

\\ random exponent for the local samplers: a mixture concentrated near 0 (uniform on [-3, 3] with probability 1/2,
\\ geometric |k| with a random sign with probability 1/4) and uniform on [-km, km] with probability 1/4; the wide
\\ component reaches deep valuations, the narrow ones keep the rare regions near valuation 0 likely
rich_randexp(km) =
{
  my(t = random(4), k = 0);
  if (t <= 1, return(random(7) - 3));
  if (t == 2, while (k < km && random(2), k++); return(if (random(2), k, -k)));
  random(2 * km + 1) - km;
}

\\ random x in K, spread over K_v: pi^k r with k drawn by rich_randexp(4 e_v + 4) and r a random integral element
\\ modulo p^10
rich_randx(F, P) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), n = poldegree(nfK.pol), p, k, r, j, km);
  if (mapget(P, "type") == 0, j = random(5); return((random(2 * 10^4 + 1) - 10^4) / (1 + random(10^j))));
  p = mapget(P, "p"); km = mapget(P, "pr").e; km = 4 * km + 4; k = rich_randexp(km);
  r = if (n == 1, random(p^10), nfbasistoalg(nfK, vectorv(n, i, random(p^10))));
  rich_Kelt(F, mapget(P, "piK")^k * r);
}

\\ global representatives of the nontrivial classes of K_v^x / squares: elements of O_K with small coordinates on
\\ the integral basis and v_pr in {0, 1}, one per class, found by a random search over growing boxes; all the
\\ classes when there are at most maxn, else maxn distinct ones. Small representatives keep the defining polynomial of
\\ K(sqrt e) small (the cost of every step of rich_quadpoints depends on it), and v(e) in {0, 1} is what the
\\ samplers of rich_try_quad and rich_quadpoints assume.
rich_Kvclasses(F, P, maxn = 63) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), n = poldegree(nfK.pol), pr = mapget(P, "pr"), p = mapget(P, "p"), S, m, want,
     seen = Map(), reps = List(), a, c, bx = 1, tries = 0);
  S = rich_sqinit(nfK, pr); m = 1 + #S[4]; want = min(2^m - 1, maxn);
  while (#reps < want,
    tries++; if (tries % (40 * want) == 0, bx++);
    a = if (n == 1, random(2 * bx * p^2 + 1) - bx * p^2, nfbasistoalg(nfK, vectorv(n, i, random(2 * bx + 1) - bx)));
    if (a == 0 || nfeltval(nfK, a, pr) > 1, next);
    c = rich_sqcoord(nfK, S, a);
    if (c == 0 || mapisdefined(seen, c), next);
    mapput(seen, c, 1); listput(reps, rich_Kelt(F, a)));
  Vec(reps);
}

\\ the quadratic extension M = K(sqrt e) of K (e in K not a square in K_v), with its prime above the finite place P;
\\ rnfequation is applied to e1 = e dn^2, integral (a non-integral x^2 - e gives a non-monic polynomial that nfinit
\\ silently changes); the absolute polynomial of M is reduced by polredbest (arithmetic in M is the main cost of the
\\ global quadratic samplers)
rich_quadfield(F, P, e) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), p = mapget(P, "p"), pr = mapget(P, "pr"), eq, rb, Mpol, zr, nfM, aM, bM, WM, dn, e1);
  dn = denominator(nfalgtobasis(nfK, rich_Kelt(F, e))); e1 = rich_Kelt(F, e) * dn^2;
  eq = rnfequation(nfK, x^2 - if (type(e1) == "t_POLMOD", lift(e1), e1), 1);
  rb = polredbest(eq[1], 1);
  Mpol = subst(rb[1], 'x, 'zM); zr = subst(lift(rb[2]), 'x, Mod('zM, Mpol));
  nfM = nfinit([Mpol, [p]]);
  aM = subst(lift(eq[2]), 'x, zr); bM = (zr - eq[3] * aM) / dn;
  rich_chk(bM^2 == subst(lift(rich_Kelt(F, e)), variable(mapget(F, "Kpol")), aM), "rich_quadfield: sqrt(e)");
  WM = rich_above(nfK, nfM, b -> subst(lift(b), variable(mapget(F, "Kpol")), aM), pr);
  rich_chk(#WM == 1 && WM[1].e * WM[1].f == 2 * pr.e * pr.f, "K_v(sqrt e) is not a quadratic field");
  [x^2 - e, nfM, aM, bM, WM, 0, -e];
}

rich_KtoM(F, Q, a) = { my(b = rich_Kelt(F, a)); if (type(b) == "t_POLMOD", b = lift(b)); subst(b, variable(mapget(F, "Kpol")), Q[3]); }

\\ one quadratic sample on the curve R in the field Q = rich_quadfield(...): kappa value of the pair of conjugate
\\ points with x = al + be * sqrt(e) (al, be random in K), or 0 if f(x) is not a square in M_W
rich_try_quad(F, R, P, Q) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), n = poldegree(nfK.pol), p = mapget(P, "p"), pi = mapget(P, "piK"), al, be, x1, fx, tr,
     nm, u, g, k, km, rnd, j);
  km = mapget(P, "pr").e; km = 4 * km + 4; k = rich_randexp(km);
  al = rich_Kelt(F, pi^k * rich_rndK(nfK, n, p));
  \\ v(be) = v(al) half of the time: then x = pi^k (r1 + r2 sqrt e) is a random element of pi^k Z_p[sqrt e], which is
  \\ pi^k O_W for p odd since v(e) is 0 or 1 (rich_Kvclasses); otherwise a small or a mixed offset
  j = random(4); j = if (j <= 1, 0, j == 2, random(5) - 2, rich_randexp(km));
  be = rich_Kelt(F, pi^(k + j) * rich_rndK(nfK, n, p));
  if (be == 0, return(0));
  x1 = rich_KtoM(F, Q, al) + rich_KtoM(F, Q, be) * Q[4];
  fx = subst(Pol(apply(c -> rich_KtoM(F, Q, c), Vec(mapget(R, "f"))), 'x), 'x, x1);
  if (fx == 0, return(0));
  for (i = 1, #Q[5], if (!rich_nfsq(Q[2], Q[5][i], fx), return(0)));
  tr = 2 * al - Q[6] * be; nm = al^2 - Q[6] * al * be + Q[7] * be^2;
  u = x^2 - tr * x + nm;
  g = polresultant(rich_toLx(F, u), mapget(R, "G2L"), 'x);
  if (g == 0, return(0));
  g;
}

\\ residue representatives: q = N(pr) elements of O_K, pairwise distinct modulo pr
rich_resreps(F, pr) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), mp, g, L, i = 0);
  if (pr.f == 1, return(vector(pr.p, j, j - 1)));
  mp = nfmodprinit(nfK, pr); g = ffgen(nfmodpr(nfK, variable(nfK.pol), mp));
  L = vector(pr.p^pr.f);
  forvec (c = vector(pr.f, j, [0, pr.p - 1]), i++; L[i] = rich_Kelt(F, rich_alg(nfK, nfmodprlift(nfK, sum(j = 1, pr.f, c[j] * g^(j - 1)), mp))));
  L;
}

\\ reduction data at the prime W of the field nfX (nfK, or nfM for a quadratic field; toX maps K into it):
\\ [modpr, uniformiser of W, Map (image in the residue field k_W).pol -> index in reps, images of reps]
rich_reddata(F, nfX, W, reps, toX) =
{
  my(mp = nfmodprinit(nfX, W), vp, imgs, tab = Map());
  vp = if (W.e == 1, W.p, nfbasistoalg(nfX, W.gen[2]));
  rich_chk(nfeltval(nfX, vp, W) == 1, "uniformiser in rich_reddata");
  imgs = vector(#reps, i, nfmodpr(nfX, toX(reps[i]), mp));
  for (i = 1, #reps, mapput(tab, imgs[i].pol, i));
  [mp, vp, tab, imgs];
}

\\ roots in k_W of the reduction of sum_i cs[i] T^(i-1) scaled by W^(-min valuation) (cs in nfX, not all zero)
rich_redroots(nfX, W, RD, cs) =
{
  my(v0 = oo, red, Pb, fa, rts = List());
  foreach (cs, c, if (c != 0, v0 = min(v0, nfeltval(nfX, c, W))));
  red = vector(#cs, i, nfmodpr(nfX, cs[i] / RD[2]^v0, RD[1]));
  Pb = Polrev(red, 'x);
  if (poldegree(Pb) <= 0, return([]));
  fa = factor(Pb);
  for (i = 1, #fa~, if (poldegree(fa[i, 1]) == 1, listput(rts, -polcoef(fa[i, 1], 0) / polcoef(fa[i, 1], 1))));
  Vec(rts);
}

\\ Taylor coefficients [P(a), P'(a), P''(a)/2, ...] of P in x at a
rich_taylor(P, a) =
{
  my(n = poldegree(P, 'x), Q = P, c = vector(n + 1));
  for (i = 0, n, c[i + 1] = subst(Q, 'x, a); Q = deriv(Q, 'x) / (i + 1));
  c;
}

\\ margins of a disc for the square class of a function with value c0 at the centre and higher Taylor terms cs
\\ (already multiplied by the powers of pi^m), at the primes Ws of nf: [min_w (min_i v_w(cs_i) - v_w(c0)
\\ - 2 v_w(2) - 1), min_w min_i (v_w(cs_i) - v_w(c0))]. The class is constant on the disc when the first entry is
\\ >= 0 (sufficient: the ratio to c0 lies in 1 + 4 pi O); the disc holds no zero and the valuation is constant when
\\ the second entry is >= 1. A zero at the centre gives [-oo, -oo] (as -10^6).
rich_margin(nf, Ws, c0, cs) =
{
  my(m1 = 10^6, m2 = 10^6, v0, d);
  if (c0 == 0, return([-10^6, -10^6]));
  foreach (Ws, w,
    v0 = nfeltval(nf, c0, w);
    foreach (cs, c, if (c != 0, d = nfeltval(nf, c, w) - v0; m2 = min(m2, d); m1 = min(m1, d - 2 * if (w.p == 2, w.e, 0) - 1))));
  [m1, m2];
}

\\ random element of O_K modulo p^10 (integral basis coordinates)
rich_randint(F, p) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), n = poldegree(nfK.pol));
  rich_Kelt(F, if (n == 1, random(p^10), nfbasistoalg(nfK, vectorv(n, i, random(p^10)))));
}

\\ systematic search of the rational points of R over K_v by a tree of residue discs, breadth first: x = a + pi^m t
\\ (t in O_v) for x in O_v, and x = 1/s, s = a + pi^m t in pi O_v for v(x) < 0 (side 2, with f*(s) = s^6 f(1/s) and
\\ G2*(s) = s^2 G2(1/s), which have the square classes of f(x) and G2(x)). A disc on which the classes of f and G2
\\ are constant (rich_margin, sufficient test) gives one point (none if f is a nonsquare there); a disc with no zero
\\ of f or G2 but not yet constant (possible only above 2) gives nsamp random points; other discs are refined, down
\\ to depth maxdepth, where the centre is kept. Returns candidate points x in K (the caller checks that f(x) is a
\\ nonzero square). The search is not claimed to be complete (depth and node caps): completeness of the local
\\ image is certified by the duality stopping rule only.
rich_ratpoints(F, R, P, maxdepth = -1, maxnodes = 4000, nsamp = 8, nrand = 32) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), nfL = mapget(F, "nfL"), pr = mapget(P, "pr"), W = mapget(P, "W"), pi = mapget(P, "piK"),
     reps = rich_resreps(F, pr), f = mapget(R, "f"), G2 = mapget(R, "G2L"), polys, stack, out = List(), nodes = 0,
     nd, a, m, sd, cf, cg, pim, pimL, mf, mg, pt, head = 1, e2 = if (pr.p == 2, pr.e, 0), p = pr.p, RD = 0);
  if (maxdepth < 0, maxdepth = 4 * e2 + 6 + min(20, abs(nfeltval(nfK, poldisc(f), pr))));
  polys = [[f, G2], [Pol(vector(7, i, polcoef(f, i - 1, 'x)), 'x), Pol(vector(3, i, polcoef(G2, i - 1, 'x)), 'x)]];
  \\ the point of the disc with parameter t (s = 0 on side 2 is the point at infinity: not returned)
  stack = List([[0, 0, 1], [0, 1, 2]]);
  while (head <= #stack && nodes < maxnodes,
    nd = stack[head]; head++; nodes++;
    a = nd[1]; m = nd[2]; sd = nd[3]; pim = pi^m; pimL = rich_KtoL(F, pim);
    cf = rich_taylor(polys[sd][1], a);
    mf = rich_margin(nfK, [pr], cf[1], vector(#cf - 1, i, cf[i + 1] * pim^i));
    if (mf[1] >= 0 && !rich_nfsq(nfK, pr, cf[1]), next);
    cg = rich_taylor(polys[sd][2], rich_KtoL(F, a));
    mg = rich_margin(nfL, W, cg[1], vector(#cg - 1, i, cg[i + 1] * pimL^i));
    if (sd == 2 && a == 0, mf = [min(mf[1], -1), min(mf[2], 0)]);
    if (mf[1] >= 0 && mg[1] >= 0, listput(out, rich_rp_pt(F, pi, sd, a, m, 0)); next);
    if (mf[2] >= 1 && mg[2] >= 1,
      for (k = 1, nsamp, my(z = rich_rp_pt(F, pi, sd, a, m, rich_randint(F, p))); if (z != [], listput(out, z)));
      next);
    if (m >= maxdepth, my(z = rich_rp_pt(F, pi, sd, a, m, if (sd == 2 && a == 0, 1, 0))); if (z != [], listput(out, z)); next);
    \\ children: all residues when q <= 64; else the residues where the reduction of f(a + pi^m t) (scaled) vanishes
    \\ (the other children hold no zero of f, hence none of G2, and are leaves when p is odd) plus nrand random ones
    if (#reps <= 64,
      foreach (reps, r, listput(stack, [rich_Kelt(F, a + pim * r), m + 1, sd]))
    ,
      if (RD == 0, RD = rich_reddata(F, nfK, pr, reps, z -> z));
      my(ch = Map(), i);
      foreach (rich_redroots(nfK, pr, RD, vector(#cf, j, cf[j] * pim^(j - 1))), z,
        if (mapisdefined(RD[3], z.pol, &i), mapput(ch, i, 1)));
      if (sd == 2 && a == 0, mapput(ch, 1, 1));
      for (k = 1, nrand, mapput(ch, 1 + random(#reps), 1));
      foreach (Vec(ch), j, listput(stack, [rich_Kelt(F, a + pim * reps[j]), m + 1, sd]))));
  rich_lastnodes = [nodes, head <= #stack];
  Vec(out);
}

\\ systematic search of the quadratic points of R over the field M_W = K_v(sqrt e) (Q = rich_quadfield(...)), by a
\\ breadth first tree of polydiscs in (al, be), x = al + be sqrt(e): al = a + pi^m t1, be = b + pi^m t2 (t1, t2 in
\\ O_v), from m = -v(2) (O_K[sqrt e] / 2 contains O_W since v(e) is 0 or 1); side 2 is x = 1/s with f*, G2* as in
\\ rich_ratpoints. kappa of the pair {x, sigma x} is Res(u_x, G2) = G2(x) G2(sigma x), a polynomial Rt in (t1, t2)
\\ over L (from Res(X^2 - 2 al X + al^2 - e be^2, G2)). On a polydisc where the class of f(x) in M_W^x / squares
\\ (Taylor test in M) and the class of Rt (test on its coefficients at the primes of L above v) are constant and f(x)
\\ is a square: one kappa value (a leaf). Polydiscs with no zero of f or Rt but not yet constant (only above 2):
\\ nsamp random points, each checked. Others are refined, down to depth maxdepth (centres with be != 0 kept if f is a
\\ square there). Returns kappa values, each the kappa value of genuine quadratic points of R over K_v.
rich_quadpoints(F, R, P, Q, maxdepth = -1, maxnodes = 3000, nsamp = 8, nrand = 32) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), nfL = mapget(F, "nfL"), pr = mapget(P, "pr"), W = mapget(P, "W"), pi = mapget(P, "piK"),
     reps = rich_resreps(F, pr), f = mapget(R, "f"), G2 = mapget(R, "G2L"), e = -Q[7], nfM = Q[2], WM = Q[5], sq = Q[4],
     eL, polys, stack, out = List(), nodes = 0, nd, a, b, m, sd, g, pim, pimM, x0, c, A, Bq, s, n, Rt, r00, mf, mg,
     e2 = if (pr.p == 2, pr.e, 0), toM, fs, m0, head = 1, p = pr.p, cs, RDM = 0, sbar);
  if (maxdepth < 0, maxdepth = 3 * e2 + 4 + min(12, abs(nfeltval(nfK, poldisc(f), pr))));
  m0 = -e2;
  fs = Pol(vector(7, i, polcoef(f, i - 1, 'x)), 'x);
  polys = [[rich_toMx(F, Q, f), vector(3, i, polcoef(G2, i - 1, 'x))], [rich_toMx(F, Q, fs), vector(3, i, polcoef(G2, 3 - i, 'x))]];
  eL = rich_KtoL(F, e);
  stack = List([[0, 0, m0, 1], [0, 0, m0, 2]]);
  while (head <= #stack && nodes < maxnodes,
    nd = stack[head]; head++; nodes++;
    a = nd[1]; b = nd[2]; m = nd[3]; sd = nd[4]; pim = pi^m; pimM = rich_KtoM(F, Q, pim);
    x0 = rich_KtoM(F, Q, a) + rich_KtoM(F, Q, b) * sq;
    c = rich_taylor(polys[sd][1], x0);
    mf = rich_margin(nfM, WM, c[1], vector(#c - 1, i, c[i + 1] * pimM^i));
    if (mf[1] >= 0 && !rich_nfsq(nfM, WM[1], c[1]), next);
    \\ Rt: kappa as a polynomial in t1, t2, with g = [g0, g1, g2] for G2 (or G2*) = g2 X^2 + g1 X + g0
    g = polys[sd][2];
    A = rich_KtoL(F, a) + rich_KtoL(F, pim) * rich_qa; Bq = rich_KtoL(F, b) + rich_KtoL(F, pim) * rich_qb;
    s = 2 * A; n = A^2 - eL * Bq^2;
    Rt = g[3]^2 * n^2 + g[3] * g[2] * n * s + g[3] * g[1] * (s^2 - 2 * n) + g[2]^2 * n + g[2] * g[1] * s + g[1]^2;
    r00 = subst(subst(Rt, rich_qa, 0), rich_qb, 0);
    cs = List();
    for (i = 0, 4, for (j = 0, 4 - i, if (i + j > 0, listput(cs, polcoef(polcoef(Rt, i, rich_qa), j, rich_qb)))));
    mg = rich_margin(nfL, W, r00, Vec(cs));
    if (mf[1] >= 0 && mg[1] >= 0, listput(out, r00); next);
    if (mf[2] >= 1 && mg[2] >= 1,
      for (k = 1, nsamp,
        my(t1 = rich_randint(F, p), t2 = rich_randint(F, p), fx, val);
        if (b + pim * t2 == 0, next);
        fx = subst(polys[sd][1], 'x, x0 + pimM * (rich_KtoM(F, Q, t1) + rich_KtoM(F, Q, t2) * sq));
        if (fx == 0 || !rich_nfsq(nfM, WM[1], fx), next);
        val = subst(subst(Rt, rich_qa, rich_KtoL(F, t1)), rich_qb, rich_KtoL(F, t2));
        if (val != 0, listput(out, val)));
      next);
    if (m >= maxdepth,
      if (b != 0 && r00 != 0 && c[1] != 0 && rich_nfsq(nfM, WM[1], c[1]), listput(out, r00));
      next);
    \\ children: all q^2 residue pairs when q <= 16; else the pairs (r1, r2) with r1 + r2 sqrt(e) a root in k_W of the
    \\ reduction of f(x0 + pi^m T) (scaled), plus nrand random pairs
    if (#reps <= 16,
      foreach (reps, r1, foreach (reps, r2, listput(stack, [rich_Kelt(F, a + pim * r1), rich_Kelt(F, b + pim * r2), m + 1, sd])))
    ,
      if (RDM == 0, RDM = rich_reddata(F, nfM, WM[1], reps, z -> rich_KtoM(F, Q, z)); sbar = nfmodpr(nfM, sq, RDM[1]));
      my(ch = Map(), i);
      foreach (rich_redroots(nfM, WM[1], RDM, vector(#c, j, c[j] * pimM^(j - 1))), z,
        for (j = 1, #reps, if (mapisdefined(RDM[3], (z - RDM[4][j] * sbar).pol, &i), mapput(ch, [i, j], 1))));
      for (k = 1, nrand, mapput(ch, [1 + random(#reps), 1 + random(#reps)], 1));
      foreach (Vec(ch), ij, listput(stack, [rich_Kelt(F, a + pim * reps[ij[1]]), rich_Kelt(F, b + pim * reps[ij[2]]), m + 1, sd]))));
  rich_lastnodes = [nodes, head <= #stack];
  Vec(out);
}

\\ local solubility of y^2 = f(x) (f in K[x] with K = nf.pol, degree 5 or 6, squarefree) at the prime pr, with a
\\ proof either way. Returns [1, x0] (x0 in K with f(x0) a nonzero square at pr; x0 = "oo" for a rational point at
\\ infinity; x0 = [a] when Hensel's lemma gives a root of f in K_v near a), [0] (no point: every disc of the tree of
\\ residue discs of P^1(K_v) carries a constant nonsquare class of f, the test being the sufficient Taylor test of
\\ rich_margin), or [-1] (undecided within maxdepth / maxnodes).
rich_locsolv(nf, pr, f, maxdepth = 40, maxnodes = 20000) =
{
  my(p = pr.p, reps, pi, stack, head = 1, nodes = 0, nd, a, m, sd, cf, mg, polys, v0, v1, undec = 0, K = nf.pol,
     alg = (z -> if (poldegree(K) == 1, z, Mod(z, K))), mp, g, i = 0);
  if (poldegree(f) == 5, return([1, "oo"]));
  if (rich_nfsq(nf, pr, pollead(f)), return([1, "oo"]));
  if (pr.f == 1, reps = vector(p, j, j - 1),
    mp = nfmodprinit(nf, pr); g = ffgen(nfmodpr(nf, variable(K), mp)); reps = vector(p^pr.f);
    forvec (c = vector(pr.f, j, [0, p - 1]), i++; reps[i] = alg(lift(rich_alg(nf, nfmodprlift(nf, sum(j = 1, pr.f, c[j] * g^(j - 1)), mp))))));
  pi = alg(if (pr.e == 1, p, lift(nfbasistoalg(nf, pr.gen[2]))));
  rich_chk(nfeltval(nf, pi, pr) == 1, "uniformiser in rich_locsolv");
  polys = [f, Pol(vector(7, j, polcoef(f, j - 1, 'x)), 'x)];
  stack = List([[0, 0, 1], [0, 1, 2]]);
  while (head <= #stack,
    if (nodes >= maxnodes, return([-1]));
    nd = stack[head]; head++; nodes++;
    a = nd[1]; m = nd[2]; sd = nd[3];
    cf = rich_taylor(polys[sd], a);
    if (cf[1] != 0 && rich_nfsq(nf, pr, cf[1]) && !(sd == 2 && a == 0), return([1, if (sd == 1, a, 1 / a)]));
    \\ Hensel for g(t) = f(a + t) (or f*(a + t)) made primitive in O_v[t]: v(g(0)) - c > 2 (v(g'(0)) - c), c the
    \\ minimal valuation of the coefficients of g, gives a root of f (or f*) in K_v, hence a point with y = 0
    if (cf[1] == 0, return([1, [a, sd]]));
    if (cf[2] != 0,
      my(c = oo); foreach (cf, t, if (t != 0, c = min(c, nfeltval(nf, t, pr))));
      v0 = nfeltval(nf, cf[1], pr); v1 = nfeltval(nf, cf[2], pr);
      if (v0 + c > 2 * v1, return([1, [a, sd]])));
    mg = rich_margin(nf, [pr], cf[1], vector(#cf - 1, j, cf[j + 1] * pi^(m * j)));
    if (mg[1] >= 0, next);
    if (m >= maxdepth, undec = 1; next);
    foreach (reps, r, listput(stack, [a + pi^m * r, m + 1, sd])));
  if (undec, [-1], [0]);
}

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- local model at a finite place of degree one
\\ K_v = Q_p[Y]/(E(Y)) with E Eisenstein of degree e = e(v/p) (f(v/p) = 1): Y is the image of a global uniformiser
\\ pw (v_pr(pw) = 1, v_q(pw) = 0 at the other primes q above p, pw a generator of K) and E is the Eisenstein factor of
\\ its characteristic polynomial over Q_p. Elements of K_v are t_POLMOD in rich_lY over t_PADIC (PARI tracks the
\\ precision). sum_{i<e} c_i Y^i has valuation min_i (e v_p(c_i) + i) (the terms have distinct valuations). Elements
\\ with integer coordinates c_i are exact and lift exactly to the global element sum c_i pw^i: the local trees use
\\ such centres, so every point they return is a point of K (or of K(sqrt e)) and is checked globally by the caller.
\\ Quadratic extensions of K_v (the fields K_v(sqrt dl) of the quadratic trees, and L_v = L tensor K_v) are relative:
\\ t_POLMOD in rich_lS (resp. rich_lT) over K_v. Only the search uses the local model; the square classes of the
\\ Kummer values (and hence the local images and the count) are computed globally as before.
rich_lT = varlower("rich_lT", 'x); rich_lS = varlower("rich_lS", rich_lT); rich_lY = varlower("rich_lY", rich_lS);

\\ an element of K_v given as a t_POL of degree <= 0 in a variable other than rich_lY (as returned by subst of a
\\ constant polynomial) is replaced by its constant term; rich_lv_val would misread the wrapper
rich_lv_unwrap(z) =
{
  while (type(z) == "t_POL" && variable(z) != rich_lY,
    rich_chk(poldegree(z) <= 0, "rich_lv_unwrap: not an element of K_v");
    z = polcoef(z, 0));
  z;
}

\\ lower bound for the valuation of z in K_v: [v, exact] (exact = 0 when the minimum sits on a coefficient known to be
\\ 0 only to its precision: then z = 0 to that precision and v is a lower bound); [oo, 1] for an exact 0
rich_lv_val(LV, z) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), c, best = oo, ex = 1, t);
  z = rich_lv_unwrap(z);
  while (type(z) == "t_POLMOD", my(vm = variable(z.mod)); z = lift(z); if (vm == rich_lY, break); z = rich_lv_unwrap(z));
  for (i = 0, e - 1,
    c = polcoef(z, i, rich_lY);
    if (type(c) != "t_PADIC" && c == 0, next);
    t = e * valuation(c, p) + i;
    if (t < best, best = t; ex = (c != 0)));
  [best, ex];
}

\\ inverse of a unit of K_v (Newton iteration y <- y (2 - u y))
rich_lv_uinv(LV, u) =
{
  my(y, t);
  u = rich_lv_unwrap(u); y = 1 / polcoef(lift(u), 0, rich_lY);
  for (i = 1, 64,
    t = rich_lv_val(LV, u * y - 1);
    if (!t[2] || t[1] == oo, return(y));
    y = y * (2 - u * y));
  error("richelot: rich_lv_uinv does not converge");
}

\\ z / pi^k exactly (0 <= k <= v(z)), with no loss of relative precision: z / p^q times (pi^e / p)^(-q), then a shift
\\ by r = k mod e using p = pi^e epsinv^(-1)... (coefficients below Y^r are divisible by p)
rich_lv_divpi(LV, z, k) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), E = mapget(LV, "E"), q = k \ e, r = k % e, w, hi, lo, c);
  z = rich_lv_unwrap(z);
  if (k == 0, return(z));
  w = z / p^q;
  if (q, w *= mapget(LV, "epsinv")^q);
  if (r == 0, return(w));
  if (type(w) != "t_POLMOD", w = Mod(w, E)); w = lift(w);
  hi = sum(i = r, e - 1, polcoef(w, i, rich_lY) * rich_lY^(i - r));
  lo = sum(i = 0, r - 1, polcoef(w, i, rich_lY) / p * rich_lY^(i + e - r));
  Mod(hi, E) + Mod(lo, E) * mapget(LV, "epsinv");
}

\\ is z a nonzero square in K_v: 1, 0, or -1 when the precision does not decide. p odd: Legendre symbol of the unit
\\ part (f = 1). p = 2 (residue field F2, units are 1 mod pi): multiply u by (1 + Y^(j/2))^2 while v(u - 1) = j is even
\\ and < 2e (this raises v(u - 1)); u is a square iff v(u - 1) reaches 2e + 1 (odd j < 2e, or j = 2e: not a square)
rich_lv_issq(LV, z) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), Yv = mapget(LV, "Y"), vz, u, t, j);
  z = rich_lv_unwrap(z);
  vz = rich_lv_val(LV, z);
  if (!vz[2], return(-1));
  if (vz[1] == oo, return(0));
  if (vz[1] % 2, return(0));
  u = rich_lv_divpi(LV, z, vz[1]);
  if (p != 2, return(kronecker(truncate(polcoef(lift(u), 0, rich_lY)) % p, p) == 1));
  for (it = 1, 2 * e + 2,
    t = rich_lv_val(LV, u - 1); j = t[1];
    if (j >= 2 * e + 1, return(1));
    if (!t[2], return(-1));
    if (j % 2 || j == 2 * e, return(0));
    u *= (1 + Yv^(j / 2))^2);
  error("richelot: rich_lv_issq");
}

\\ a square root of the square z in K_v (working precision): u = z / pi^v, a unit w with u w^2 = 1 mod pi^(2e+1) (p = 2)
\\ or the constant coefficient (p odd), then Newton for u1^(-1/2), u1 = u w^2: r <- r (3 - u1 r^2) / 2;
\\ sqrt(z) = pi^(v/2) u r w (no division by w needed)
rich_lv_sqrt(LV, z) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), Yv = mapget(LV, "Y"), vz, u, w = 1, t, j, u1, r);
  z = rich_lv_unwrap(z);
  vz = rich_lv_val(LV, z); rich_chk(vz[2] && vz[1] < oo && vz[1] % 2 == 0, "rich_lv_sqrt: not a square");
  u = rich_lv_divpi(LV, z, vz[1]);
  if (p == 2,
    for (it = 1, 2 * e + 2,
      t = rich_lv_val(LV, u * w^2 - 1); j = t[1];
      if (j >= 2 * e + 1, break);
      rich_chk(t[2] && j % 2 == 0 && j < 2 * e, "rich_lv_sqrt: not a square");
      w *= (1 + Yv^(j / 2)));
    r = 1
  ,
    my(c0 = polcoef(lift(u), 0, rich_lY)); if (type(c0) != "t_PADIC", c0 += O(p^mapget(LV, "prec")));
    r = 1 / sqrt(c0));
  u1 = u * w^2;
  for (i = 1, 64,
    t = rich_lv_val(LV, u1 * r^2 - 1);
    if (!t[2] || t[1] == oo, return(Yv^(vz[1] / 2) * u * r * w));
    r = r * (3 - u1 * r^2) / 2);
  error("richelot: rich_lv_sqrt does not converge");
}

\\ pi^(-n) in K_v (n >= 0): pi^(e q - n) (epsinv / p)^q with q = ceil(n / e), since pi^e = p / epsinv
rich_lv_pineg(LV, n) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), q = ceil(n / e));
  mapget(LV, "Y")^(e * q - n) * (mapget(LV, "epsinv") / mapget(LV, "p"))^q;
}

\\ quadratic extension K_v(sqrt dl) (dl in K_v, not 0, any valuation): [dl, fW, eW, th0, th1, sd, var]. Field case
\\ (sd = 0): f(W/v), e(W/v), and th = th0 + th1 sqrt(dl) with O_W = O_v[th]. Split case (dl a square): sd = sqrt(dl)
\\ in K_v, fW = eW = 1. var: rich_lS (quadratic trees) or rich_lT (L_v). With k = v(dl) \ 2 and u = dl / pi^(2k),
\\ sqrt(u) = sqrt(dl) pi^(-k): v(u) = 1 (ramified) or p odd (unramified): th = sqrt(u); p = 2, u a unit: w with
\\ u w^2 = 1 + eps and j = v(eps) odd < 2e (ramified: th = (w sqrt(u) - 1) / pi^((j-1)/2) is a root of an Eisenstein
\\ polynomial over O_v) or j = 2e (unramified: th = (w sqrt(u) - 1) / pi^e reduces to a root of Y^2 + Y + 1).
rich_lv_quad(LV, dl, var = rich_lS) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), Yv = mapget(LV, "Y"), vd, s, u, w = 1, t, j, jj, k, pk, pij);
  vd = rich_lv_val(LV, dl); rich_chk(vd[2] && vd[1] < oo, "rich_lv_quad: dl = 0 to precision");
  s = rich_lv_issq(LV, dl); rich_chk(s >= 0, "rich_lv_quad: precision");
  if (s == 1, return([dl, 1, 1, 0, 0, rich_lv_sqrt(LV, dl), var]));
  k = vd[1] \ 2; pk = rich_lv_pineg(LV, k);
  if (vd[1] % 2, return([dl, 1, 2, 0, pk, 0, var]));
  if (p != 2, return([dl, 2, 1, 0, pk, 0, var]));
  u = rich_lv_divpi(LV, dl, vd[1]);
  for (it = 1, 2 * e + 2,
    t = rich_lv_val(LV, u * w^2 - 1); j = t[1];
    rich_chk(t[2] && j <= 2 * e, "rich_lv_quad: square");
    if (j % 2 || j == 2 * e, break);
    w *= (1 + Yv^(j / 2)));
  jj = if (j == 2 * e, e, (j - 1) / 2);
  pij = rich_lv_pineg(LV, jj);
  [dl, if (j == 2 * e, 2, 1), if (j == 2 * e, 1, 2), -pij, w * pk * pij, 0, var];
}

\\ F2 coordinates of z in K_v^x / squares (f = 1) in the basis pi, 1 + pi^j (j odd < 2e), 5 (p = 2), or pi and a
\\ nonsquare unit (p odd): the greedy reduction of the unit part (divide by 1 + pi^j at odd levels j < 2e, multiply by
\\ (1 + pi^(j/2))^2 at even levels, divide by 5 at level 2e) ends in 1 + pi^(2e+1) O, which consists of squares.
\\ Returns 0 when the precision does not decide.
rich_lv_sqcoord(LV, z) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), Yv = mapget(LV, "Y"), vz, u, t, j, c);
  z = rich_lv_unwrap(z);
  vz = rich_lv_val(LV, z); if (!vz[2] || vz[1] == oo, return(0));
  u = rich_lv_divpi(LV, z, vz[1]);
  if (p != 2, return([vz[1] % 2, kronecker(truncate(polcoef(lift(u), 0, rich_lY)) % p, p) != 1]));
  c = vector(e + 2); c[1] = vz[1] % 2;
  for (it = 1, 4 * e + 4,
    t = rich_lv_val(LV, u - 1); j = t[1];
    if (j >= 2 * e + 1, return(c));
    if (!t[2], return(0));
    if (j % 2, c[2 + (j - 1) / 2] = 1; u *= mapget(LV, "uinvs")[(j + 1) / 2]; next);
    if (j == 2 * e, c[e + 2] = 1; u /= 5; next);
    u *= (1 + Yv^(j / 2))^2);
  error("richelot: rich_lv_sqcoord");
}

\\ [al, be] with z = al + be sqrt(dl) (z a t_POLMOD in var, a t_POL in var, or an element of K_v; subst of a constant
\\ polynomial returns a t_POL of degree 0 in the variable substituted, which is unwrapped here)
rich_lv_ab(Qd, z) =
{
  if (type(z) == "t_POLMOD" && variable(z.mod) == Qd[7], z = lift(z));
  if (type(z) == "t_POL" && variable(z) == Qd[7],
    if (poldegree(z) >= 2, z = z % (Qd[7]^2 - Qd[1]));
    return([rich_lv_unwrap(polcoef(z, 0, Qd[7])), rich_lv_unwrap(polcoef(z, 1, Qd[7]))]));
  [rich_lv_unwrap(z), 0];
}

\\ valuations of z at the places of the quadratic algebra Qd (normalised: v_W(pi_W) = 1): vector of [v, exact]
rich_lv_qvals(LV, Qd, z) =
{
  my(ab = rich_lv_ab(Qd, z), t);
  if (Qd[6] != 0, return([rich_lv_val(LV, ab[1] + Qd[6] * ab[2]), rich_lv_val(LV, ab[1] - Qd[6] * ab[2])]));
  t = rich_lv_val(LV, ab[1]^2 - Qd[1] * ab[2]^2);
  if (t[2] && t[1] < oo, rich_chk(t[1] % Qd[2] == 0, "rich_lv_qvals: norm valuation"));
  [[if (t[1] == oo, oo, t[1] \ Qd[2]), t[2]]];
}

\\ is z a nonzero square in the quadratic field Qd: N(z) = m^2 in K_v and (al + m) / 2 in K_v^x2 u dl K_v^x2 (for the
\\ sign of m with the smaller valuation of al + m); 1, 0 or -1 (precision)
rich_lv_issqQ(LV, Qd, z) =
{
  my(ab = rich_lv_ab(Qd, z), nz, s, m, v1, v2, h, r1, r2);
  nz = ab[1]^2 - Qd[1] * ab[2]^2;
  s = rich_lv_issq(LV, nz); if (s <= 0, return(s));
  m = rich_lv_sqrt(LV, nz);
  v1 = rich_lv_val(LV, ab[1] + m); v2 = rich_lv_val(LV, ab[1] - m);
  if (!v1[2] && !v2[2], return(-1));
  h = if (v1[2] && (!v2[2] || v1[1] <= v2[1]), ab[1] + m, ab[1] - m) / 2;
  r1 = rich_lv_issq(LV, h); if (r1 == 1, return(1));
  r2 = rich_lv_issq(LV, h * Qd[1]); if (r2 == 1, return(1));
  if (r1 < 0 || r2 < 0, -1, 0);
}

\\ image in K_v of an element of K
rich_lv_map(LV, a) =
{
  my(c);
  if (type(a) == "t_INT" || type(a) == "t_FRAC", return(a * mapget(LV, "one")));
  c = nfalgtobasis(mapget(LV, "nfK"), a);
  sum(i = 1, #c, c[i] * mapget(LV, "zkimg")[i]);
}

rich_lv_mapx(LV, P) = Pol(apply(c -> rich_lv_map(LV, c), rich_xcoefs(P)), 'x);

\\ global lift (element of K) of an element of K_v: sum truncate(c_i) pw^i (exact for integer coordinates); with an
\\ ideal I = pr^n, the lift is replaced by a small element congruent to it modulo pr^n (rich_lv_small)
rich_lv_lift(LV, z, I = 0) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), pp = mapget(LV, "pwpow"), r);
  z = rich_lv_unwrap(z); if (type(z) == "t_POLMOD", z = lift(z));
  r = sum(i = 0, e - 1, truncate(polcoef(z, i, rich_lY)) * pp[i + 1]);
  if (I == 0, r, rich_lv_small(LV, r, I));
}

\\ an element of K congruent to a modulo I = pr^n at pr, with small coordinates on the integral basis: HNF reduction of
\\ dn a modulo dn I (dn the denominator of a), divided by dn
rich_lv_small(LV, a, I) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(LV, "nfK"), c, dn);
  if (a == 0, return(0));
  c = nfalgtobasis(nfK, a); dn = denominator(c);
  rich_Kelt_nf(nfK, nfbasistoalg(nfK, nfeltreduce(nfK, c * dn, idealmul(nfK, dn, I))) / dn);
}

\\ element of K as returned by nfbasistoalg, normalised (t_POLMOD, or a rational number when K = Q)
rich_Kelt_nf(nfK, a) = if (poldegree(nfK.pol) == 1, if (type(a) == "t_POLMOD", a = lift(a)); if (type(a) == "t_POL", polcoef(a, 0), a), a);

\\ a small global representative (integral, v_pr in {0, 1}) of the class of z in K_v^x / squares: the unit or
\\ uniformiser part u = z pi^(-2k), truncated to O(pi^(2e+3)) and lifted, then reduced modulo pr^(2e+3)
rich_lv_classrep(LV, z) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), vz, k, u, D, g);
  z = rich_lv_unwrap(z);
  vz = rich_lv_val(LV, z); rich_chk(vz[2] && vz[1] < oo, "rich_lv_classrep: z = 0 to precision");
  k = vz[1] \ 2;
  u = if (k >= 0, rich_lv_divpi(LV, z, 2 * k), z * mapget(LV, "Y")^(-2 * k));
  D = 2 + (2 * e + 3) \ e + 1;
  u = lift(u); u = sum(i = 0, e - 1, truncate(polcoef(u, i, rich_lY) + O(p^D)) * rich_lY^i);
  g = rich_lv_lift(LV, u, idealpow(mapget(LV, "nfK"), mapget(LV, "pr"), 2 * e + 3));
  rich_chk(rich_lv_sqcoord(LV, rich_lv_map(LV, g)) == rich_lv_sqcoord(LV, z), "rich_lv_classrep: class changed");
  g;
}

\\ margins of a disc (as rich_margin) at the place of K_v (Qd = 0) or at the places of the quadratic algebra Qd
rich_lv_marg(LV, Qd, c0, cs) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), vf, v0, m1 = 10^6, m2 = 10^6, vs, v2, dd);
  v2 = if (p == 2, e * if (Qd == 0, 1, Qd[3]), 0);
  v0 = rich_lv_vfv(LV, Qd, c0);
  for (w = 1, #v0, if (!v0[w][2] || v0[w][1] == oo, return([-10^6, -10^6])));
  foreach (cs, c,
    vs = rich_lv_vfv(LV, Qd, c);
    for (w = 1, #vs, if (vs[w][1] == oo, next); dd = vs[w][1] - v0[w][1]; m2 = min(m2, dd); m1 = min(m1, dd - 2 * v2 - 1)));
  [m1, m2];
}

\\ local data at the finite place P (f = 1): Map with "p", "e", "E", "Y" (the class of Y), "pw", "pwpow", "zkimg"
\\ (images of the integral basis), "epsinv" ((pi^e / p)^(-1)), "pie" (pi^e), "one", "L" (the algebra L_v), "prec"
rich_lv_init(F, P, prec = 120, tgt = 60) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), pr = mapget(P, "pr"), p = pr.p, e = pr.e, n = poldegree(nfK.pol), Kv, LV = Map(), dec,
     fa, pw, cp, fac, E = 0, Mp, r, beta, zkimg, pmin, eps, Yv);
  rich_chk(pr.f == 1, "rich_lv_init needs a prime of degree one");
  Kv = variable(nfK.pol);
  dec = idealprimedec(nfK, p);
  fa = matrix(#dec, 2, i, j, if (j == 1, dec[i], dec[i] == pr));
  pw = nfbasistoalg(nfK, idealappr(nfK, fa));
  if (n > 1, while (!issquarefree(charpoly(pw, 'x)), pw += p^2 * nfbasistoalg(nfK, vectorv(n, i, random(3) - 1))));
  if (n == 1, pw = lift(pw); if (type(pw) == "t_POL", pw = polcoef(pw, 0)));
  rich_chk(nfeltval(nfK, pw, pr) == 1, "rich_lv_init: uniformiser");
  cp = if (n == 1, 'x - pw, charpoly(pw, 'x));
  while (1,
    fac = factorpadic(cp, p, prec); E = 0;
    for (i = 1, #fac~, my(g = fac[i, 1]);
      if (poldegree(g) == e && valuation(polcoef(g, 0), p) == 1 && vecmin(vector(e, j, valuation(polcoef(g, j - 1), p))) >= 1,
        rich_chk(E == 0, "rich_lv_init: two Eisenstein factors"); E = g));
    rich_chk(E != 0, "rich_lv_init: no Eisenstein factor");
    E = subst(E, 'x, rich_lY);
    if (n == 1,
      zkimg = [Mod(1 + O(p^prec), E)]
    ,
      \\ b = r(pw) (pw generates K), then the images of the integral basis
      Mp = matrix(n, n, i, j, polcoef(lift(pw^(j - 1)), i - 1, Kv));
      r = matsolve(Mp, vectorv(n, i, i == 2));
      beta = Mod(sum(j = 1, n, r[j] * rich_lY^(j - 1)), E);
      zkimg = vector(n, i, subst(lift(nfK.zk[i]), Kv, beta) + Mod(O(p^prec), E)));
    pmin = oo;
    foreach (zkimg, z, my(zz = lift(z)); for (i = 0, e - 1, my(c = polcoef(zz, i, rich_lY)); if (type(c) == "t_PADIC", pmin = min(pmin, padicprec(c, p)))));
    if (pmin >= tgt, break);
    prec = 2 * prec + (tgt - pmin));
  Yv = Mod(rich_lY, E);
  mapput(LV, "p", p); mapput(LV, "e", e); mapput(LV, "E", E); mapput(LV, "Y", Yv); mapput(LV, "nfK", nfK); mapput(LV, "pr", pr);
  mapput(LV, "pw", pw); mapput(LV, "pwpow", vector(e, i, pw^(i - 1))); mapput(LV, "zkimg", zkimg);
  mapput(LV, "one", Mod(1 + O(p^prec), E)); mapput(LV, "prec", pmin);
  \\ pi^e = p eps, eps = -(E - Y^e) / p a unit
  eps = Mod(-(E - rich_lY^e) / p, E);
  mapput(LV, "pie", Yv^e);
  mapput(LV, "epsinv", rich_lv_uinv(LV, eps));
  rich_chk(rich_lv_val(LV, mapget(LV, "epsinv") * eps - 1)[1] >= e * (pmin - 2), "rich_lv_init: epsinv");
  if (p == 2, mapput(LV, "uinvs", vector(e, i, rich_lv_uinv(LV, 1 + Yv^(2 * i - 1)))));
  mapput(LV, "L", rich_lv_quad(LV, rich_lv_map(LV, mapget(F, "d")), rich_lT));
  LV;
}

\\ the curve over K_v: [f_v, G2_v] (f_v in K_v[x], G2_v = A_v + T B_v in L_v[x]) and the side 2 polynomials
\\ f*(s) = s^6 f(1/s), G2*(s) = s^2 G2(1/s)
rich_lv_curve(LV, R) =
{
  my(LL = mapget(LV, "L"), fv, Av, Bv, g, G2v);
  fv = rich_lv_mapx(LV, mapget(R, "f"));
  Av = rich_lv_mapx(LV, mapget(R, "A")); Bv = rich_lv_mapx(LV, mapget(R, "B"));
  g = vector(3, i, Mod(polcoef(Av, i - 1, 'x) + rich_lT * polcoef(Bv, i - 1, 'x), rich_lT^2 - LL[1]));
  G2v = Pol(Vecrev(g), 'x);
  [[fv, G2v], [Pol(vector(7, i, polcoef(fv, i - 1, 'x)), 'x), Pol(g, 'x)]];
}

\\ the element sum_{i<e} t_i p^((m+i)\e) Y^((m+i)%e) of pi^m O_v (these e monomials have valuations m, ..., m+e-1, a
\\ Z_p-basis of pi^m O_v), as an integer polynomial in Y
rich_lv_disc(LV, m, t) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"));
  sum(i = 0, e - 1, t[i + 1] * p^((m + i) \ e) * rich_lY^((m + i) % e));
}

rich_lv_rnd(LV, m) = rich_lv_disc(LV, m, vector(mapget(LV, "e"), i, random(mapget(LV, "p")^10)));

\\ quadratic fields for the local trees: first the classes of lc(f) and of f(x0), for both curves and nsample random
\\ x0 in P^1(K_v) (quadratic points near a point with x = x0 or near infinity give divisor classes close to 0: the
\\ formal group part of the images, which is most of them above 2), then the given representatives reps; one field
\\ per nontrivial class of K_v^x / squares, at most maxf; each field as a small global representative
rich_lv_fields(F, sides, P, LV, reps, nsample = 80, maxf = 96) =
{
  my(seen = Map(), out = List(), c, cands, fv, fs, X, sd, a);
  for (s = 1, 2,
    fv = rich_lv_mapx(LV, mapget(sides[s], "f")); fs = Pol(vector(7, j, polcoef(fv, j - 1, 'x)), 'x);
    cands = List([polcoef(fv, 6, 'x)]);
    for (i = 1, nsample,
      sd = random(2); a = rich_lv_rnd(LV, if (random(2), 0, random(2 * mapget(LV, "e") + 2)));
      X = Mod(a, mapget(LV, "E")) + mapget(LV, "one") - 1;
      listput(cands, subst(if (sd == 0, fv, fs), 'x, X)));
    foreach (cands, z,
      if (#out >= maxf, break);
      c = rich_lv_sqcoord(LV, z);
      if (c == 0 || c == vector(#c) || mapisdefined(seen, c), next);
      mapput(seen, c, 1); listput(out, rich_lv_classrep(LV, z))));
  foreach (reps, g,
    if (#out >= maxf, break);
    c = rich_lv_sqcoord(LV, rich_lv_map(LV, g));
    if (c == 0 || c == vector(#c) || mapisdefined(seen, c), next);
    mapput(seen, c, 1); listput(out, g));
  Vec(out);
}

\\ local version of rich_ratpoints (same output: candidate points of R over K_v, as elements of K); the tree is the
\\ same with exact centres a (integer polynomials in Y) and children a + p^(m\e) Y^(m%e) r, r = 0..p-1; the points
\\ are lifted to small elements of K congruent modulo pr^(maxdepth + 2) (same disc); the caller checks each globally
rich_lv_ratpoints(F, R, P, LV, maxdepth = -1, maxnodes = 4000, nsamp = 8) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), E = mapget(LV, "E"), LL = mapget(LV, "L"), polys = rich_lv_curve(LV, R),
     e2 = if (p == 2, e, 0), stack, head = 1, nodes = 0, out = List(), nd, a, m, sd, av, lam, cf, cg, mf, mg, pt, I);
  if (maxdepth < 0, maxdepth = 4 * e2 + 6 + min(20, abs(nfeltval(mapget(F, "nfK"), poldisc(mapget(R, "f")), mapget(P, "pr")))));
  I = idealpow(mapget(LV, "nfK"), mapget(LV, "pr"), maxdepth + 2);
  stack = List([[0, 0, 1], [0, 1, 2]]);
  while (head <= #stack && nodes < maxnodes,
    nd = stack[head]; head++; nodes++;
    a = nd[1]; m = nd[2]; sd = nd[3];
    av = Mod(a, E) + mapget(LV, "one") - 1; lam = Mod(p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), E);
    cf = rich_taylor(polys[sd][1], av);
    mf = rich_lv_marg(LV, 0, cf[1], vector(#cf - 1, i, cf[i + 1] * lam^i));
    if (mf[1] >= 0 && rich_lv_issq(LV, cf[1]) == 0, next);
    cg = rich_taylor(polys[sd][2], av);
    mg = rich_lv_marg(LV, LL, cg[1], vector(#cg - 1, i, cg[i + 1] * lam^i));
    if (sd == 2 && a == 0, mf = [min(mf[1], -1), min(mf[2], 0)]);
    if (mf[1] >= 0 && mg[1] >= 0, listput(out, rich_lv_rp_pt(LV, I, sd, a)); next);
    if (mf[2] >= 1 && mg[2] >= 1,
      for (k = 1, nsamp, my(a1 = a + rich_lv_rnd(LV, m));
        if (rich_lv_issq(LV, subst(polys[sd][1], 'x, Mod(a1, E) + mapget(LV, "one") - 1)) != 0, listput(out, rich_lv_rp_pt(LV, I, sd, a1))));
      next);
    if (m >= maxdepth, listput(out, rich_lv_rp_pt(LV, I, sd, if (sd == 2 && a == 0, p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), a))); next);
    for (r = 0, p - 1, listput(stack, [a + r * p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), m + 1, sd])));
  rich_lastnodes = [nodes, head <= #stack];
  [z | z <- Vec(out), z != []];
}

\\ global point of the quadratic field K(sqrt eg) for the local point x = a + b th (side 1) or x = 1 / (a + b th)
\\ (side 2) of Qd = K_v(sqrt dl), dl the image of eg: [al, be] in K with x = al + be sqrt(eg), or [] (s = 0); al and
\\ be (of s on side 2) are reduced modulo the ideal I = pr^n (rich_lv_small)
rich_lv_qlift(LV, Qd, eg, sd, a, b, I) =
{
  my(E = mapget(LV, "E"), al, be, nn);
  al = rich_lv_lift(LV, Mod(a, E) + Mod(b, E) * Qd[4], I); be = rich_lv_lift(LV, Mod(b, E) * Qd[5], I);
  if (sd == 1, return([al, be]));
  nn = al^2 - eg * be^2;
  if (nn == 0, return([]));
  [al / nn, -be / nn];
}

\\ local version of rich_quadpoints over Qd = rich_lv_quad(LV, image of eg): polydiscs x0 + pi^m (t1 + t2 th) with
\\ x0 = a + b th (a, b exact integer polynomials in Y, t1, t2 in O_v), which cover O_W from m = 0 since
\\ O_W = O_v[th]; side 2 is x = 1/s with s in O_W. Same leaf / sampling / refinement rules as rich_quadpoints; only
\\ points where f(x) is a square in M_W by the local test are kept. Returns global points [al, be]
\\ (x = al + be sqrt(eg), eg in K); leaf centres are reduced modulo pr^(maxdepth + 2 + |v(eg)|) (same polydisc), the
\\ random points of the far polydiscs modulo pr^(40 e) (their classes are not constant on the polydisc). The caller
\\ computes the kappa values globally and checks the points kept in the bases (rich_qcheck).
rich_lv_quadpoints(F, R, P, LV, Qd, eg, maxdepth = -1, maxnodes = 3000, nsamp = 8) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), E = mapget(LV, "E"), LL = mapget(LV, "L"), polys = rich_lv_curve(LV, R),
     one = mapget(LV, "one"), e2 = if (p == 2, e, 0), dl = Qd[1], th0 = Qd[4], th1 = Qd[5], S = Qd[7], stack,
     head = 1, nodes = 0, out = List(), nd, a, b, m, sd, lam, x0, c, mf, g, Ap, Bp, sv, nv, Rt, r00, cs, mg, toQ, sq0,
     nfK = mapget(LV, "nfK"), pr = mapget(LV, "pr"), Is, Ib);
  rich_chk(Qd[6] == 0 && th1 != 0, "rich_lv_quadpoints: Qd must be a field");
  if (maxdepth < 0, maxdepth = 3 * e2 + 4 + min(12, abs(nfeltval(nfK, poldisc(mapget(R, "f")), pr))));
  Is = idealpow(nfK, pr, maxdepth + 2 + abs(rich_lv_val(LV, dl)[1])); Ib = idealpow(nfK, pr, 40 * e);
  toQ = ((al, be) -> Mod(al + be * S, S^2 - dl));
  stack = List([[0, 0, 0, 1], [0, 0, 0, 2]]);
  while (head <= #stack && nodes < maxnodes,
    nd = stack[head]; head++; nodes++;
    a = nd[1]; b = nd[2]; m = nd[3]; sd = nd[4];
    lam = Mod(p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), E);
    x0 = toQ(Mod(a, E) + one - 1 + Mod(b, E) * th0, Mod(b, E) * th1);
    c = rich_taylor(polys[sd][1], x0);
    mf = rich_lv_marg(LV, Qd, c[1], vector(#c - 1, i, c[i + 1] * lam^i));
    sq0 = if (mf[1] >= 0, rich_lv_issqQ(LV, Qd, c[1]), -2);
    if (sq0 == 0, next);
    \\ Rt(t1, t2) = Res(X^2 - 2 A' X + A'^2 - dl B'^2, G2) with x = A' + B' sqrt(dl)
    g = vector(3, i, polcoef(polys[sd][2], i - 1, 'x));
    Ap = Mod(a, E) + one - 1 + Mod(b, E) * th0 + lam * (rich_qa + rich_qb * th0); Bp = th1 * (Mod(b, E) + lam * rich_qb);
    sv = 2 * Ap; nv = Ap^2 - dl * Bp^2;
    Rt = g[3]^2 * nv^2 + g[3] * g[2] * nv * sv + g[3] * g[1] * (sv^2 - 2 * nv) + g[2]^2 * nv + g[2] * g[1] * sv + g[1]^2;
    r00 = subst(subst(Rt, rich_qa, 0), rich_qb, 0);
    cs = List();
    for (i = 0, 4, for (j = 0, 4 - i, if (i + j > 0, listput(cs, polcoef(polcoef(Rt, i, rich_qa), j, rich_qb)))));
    mg = rich_lv_marg(LV, LL, r00, Vec(cs));
    if (mf[1] >= 0 && mg[1] >= 0, if (b != 0 && sq0 == 1, listput(out, [sd, a, b, 0])); next);
    if (mf[2] >= 1 && mg[2] >= 1,
      for (k = 1, nsamp,
        my(a1 = a + rich_lv_rnd(LV, m), b1 = b + rich_lv_rnd(LV, m), xx);
        if (b1 == 0, next);
        xx = toQ(Mod(a1, E) + one - 1 + Mod(b1, E) * th0, Mod(b1, E) * th1);
        if (rich_lv_issqQ(LV, Qd, subst(polys[sd][1], 'x, xx)) == 1, listput(out, [sd, a1, b1, 1])));
      next);
    if (m >= maxdepth, if (b != 0 && rich_lv_issqQ(LV, Qd, c[1]) == 1, listput(out, [sd, a, b, 1])); next);
    for (r1 = 0, p - 1, for (r2 = 0, p - 1,
      listput(stack, [a + r1 * p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), b + r2 * p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), m + 1, sd]))));
  rich_lastnodes = [nodes, head <= #stack];
  [z | z <- apply(o -> rich_lv_qlift(LV, Qd, eg, o[1], o[2], o[3], if (o[4], Ib, Is)), Vec(out)), z != []];
}

\\ inverse of a nonzero element of K_v (any valuation)
rich_lv_inv(LV, z) =
{
  my(v = rich_lv_val(LV, z), Yv = mapget(LV, "Y"));
  rich_chk(v[2] && v[1] < oo, "rich_lv_inv: zero to precision");
  if (v[1] >= 0, rich_lv_uinv(LV, rich_lv_divpi(LV, z, v[1])) * rich_lv_pineg(LV, v[1]),
                 rich_lv_uinv(LV, z * Yv^(-v[1])) * Yv^(-v[1]));
}

\\ inverse in the quadratic field Qd: (al - be S) / N(z)
rich_lv_invQ(LV, Qd, z) =
{
  my(ab = rich_lv_ab(Qd, z), ni = rich_lv_inv(LV, ab[1]^2 - Qd[1] * ab[2]^2));
  Mod((ab[1] - ab[2] * Qd[7]) * ni, Qd[7]^2 - Qd[1]);
}

\\ roots in K_v (Qd = 0) or in M_W (Qd a field from rich_lv_quad) of the polynomial g in x (coefficients in K_v, or in
\\ K_v[S]/(S^2 - dl)). The roots are first brought into O_W by x = pi^a x' (a from the Newton polygon of g), then
\\ found by a tree of discs x0 + pi^m O_v[th] and the Weierstrass degree of the Taylor expansion (the index of the
\\ last term of minimal valuation = the number of roots in the closed disc, over an algebraic closure): degree 0:
\\ dropped; degree 1: the root is unique, hence in K_v (resp. M_W), and Newton's method from the centre gives it
\\ (if Newton stalls, the disc is refined); degree >= 2: refined, down to maxdepth. Returns the roots found.
rich_lv_roots(LV, Qd, g, maxdepth = -1, maxnodes = 400) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), E = mapget(LV, "E"), one = mapget(LV, "one"), gd, stack, head,
     nodes = 0, out = List(), cen = List(), nd, a, b, m, lam, x0, c, vs, mn, wd, vf, toX, xn, t, ok, restart = 1, n,
     cv, rmax = -oo, sa = 0, sc = 1, zthr);
  if (maxdepth < 0, maxdepth = 6 * e + 20);
  toX = ((a, b) -> if (Qd == 0, Mod(a, E) + one - 1,
                       Mod(Mod(a, E) + one - 1 + Mod(b, E) * Qd[4] + Mod(b, E) * Qd[5] * Qd[7], Qd[7]^2 - Qd[1])));
  \\ scaling: the smallest root valuation is -rmax (normalised valuation of W); x = pi^sa x' puts all roots in O_W
  n = poldegree(g, 'x); cv = vector(n + 1, i, rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, polcoef(g, i - 1, 'x))[1]);
  for (i = 0, n - 1, if (cv[i + 1] < oo, rmax = max(rmax, (cv[n + 1] - cv[i + 1]) / (n - i))));
  if (rmax > 0, sa = -ceil(rmax / if (Qd == 0, 1, Qd[3])); sc = rich_lv_pipow(LV, sa); g = subst(g, 'x, sc * 'x));
  \\ a value counts as 0 only when it is 0 to at least zthr (a lower bound below zthr means lost precision)
  zthr = vecmin(vector(n + 1, i, rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, polcoef(g, i - 1, 'x))[1])) + 30 * e * if (Qd == 0, 1, Qd[3]);
  \\ a centre that is a root (to precision) is recorded, g is deflated by it and the search restarts (the roots found
  \\ in the interrupted pass are found again)
  while (restart && poldegree(g, 'x) >= 1,
    restart = 0; out = List(); gd = deriv(g, 'x); stack = List([[0, 0, 0]]); head = 1;
    while (head <= #stack && nodes < maxnodes,
      nd = stack[head]; head++; nodes++;
      a = nd[1]; b = nd[2]; m = nd[3];
      lam = Mod(p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), E);
      x0 = toX(a, b);
      c = rich_taylor(g, x0);
      t = rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, c[1]);
      if (!t[2] && t[1] < zthr, next);
      if (!t[2] || t[1] == oo,
        listput(cen, x0);
        g = sum(i = 2, #c, c[i] * ('x - x0)^(i - 2));
        restart = 1; break);
      vs = vector(#c, i, rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, c[i] * lam^(i - 1))[1]);
      mn = vecmin(vs); wd = 0;
      for (i = 1, #vs, if (vs[i] == mn, wd = i - 1));
      if (wd == 0, next);
      if (wd == 1,
        \\ a unique root in the disc: Newton from the centre (if it stalls, the disc is refined instead)
        xn = x0; ok = 0;
        for (it = 1, 80,
          my(gx = subst(g, 'x, xn), tv = rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, gx));
          if (tv[1] == oo || (!tv[2] && tv[1] >= zthr), ok = 1; break);
          if (!tv[2], break);
          xn = xn - gx * if (Qd == 0, rich_lv_inv(LV, subst(gd, 'x, xn)), rich_lv_invQ(LV, Qd, subst(gd, 'x, xn))));
        if (ok, listput(out, xn); next));
      if (m >= maxdepth, next);
      if (Qd == 0,
        for (r = 0, p - 1, listput(stack, [a + r * p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), 0, m + 1]))
      ,
        for (r1 = 0, p - 1, for (r2 = 0, p - 1,
          listput(stack, [a + r1 * p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), b + r2 * p^(m \ e) * rich_lY^(m % e), m + 1]))))));
  apply(r -> r * sc, concat(Vec(cen), Vec(out)));
}

\\ pi^n in K_v for any integer n
rich_lv_pipow(LV, n) = if (n >= 0, mapget(LV, "Y")^n, rich_lv_pineg(LV, -n));

\\ residue of z in O_W as [c0, c1] in F_p (z = a + b th, residues of a and b; c1 = 0 when Qd = 0)
rich_lv_qres(LV, Qd, z) =
{
  my(ab, bb, aa);
  if (Qd == 0, return([rich_lv_res(LV, z), 0]));
  ab = rich_lv_ab(Qd, z);
  bb = ab[2] * rich_lv_inv(LV, Qd[5]); aa = ab[1] - bb * Qd[4];
  [rich_lv_res(LV, aa), rich_lv_res(LV, bb)];
}

\\ an approximate square root of z in K_v (Qd = 0) or in the field Qd = K_v(sqrt dl) (p = 2): y with
\\ v_W(z - y^2) >= v_W(z) + j, where z = w^v u (w = pi, or th when W is ramified), and j is the level where the digit
\\ algorithm u w^2 -> u w^2 (1 + s w^(j/2))^2 stops (odd j, or j >= 2 v_W(2)); s = 1 when the residue field is F_2,
\\ s = c^2 in F_4 otherwise. Returns [y, j], or 0 when v_W(z) is odd, z = 0 to precision, or p is odd
rich_lv_approxsqrt(LV, Qd, z) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), p = mapget(LV, "p"), vf, vz, eW, fW, uni, unii, u, w, t, j, s, c, v2, one = mapget(LV, "one"));
  if (p != 2 || (Qd != 0 && Qd[6] != 0), return(0));
  vz = rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, z);
  if (!vz[2] || vz[1] == oo || vz[1] % 2, return(0));
  if (Qd == 0, eW = 1; fW = 1, eW = Qd[3]; fW = Qd[2]);
  v2 = eW * e;
  if (eW == 1,
    uni = mapget(LV, "Y"); u = z * rich_lv_pipow(LV, -vz[1])
  ,
    uni = Mod(Qd[4] + Qd[5] * Qd[7], Qd[7]^2 - Qd[1]); unii = rich_lv_invQ(LV, Qd, uni);
    u = z * if (vz[1] >= 0, unii^vz[1], uni^(-vz[1])));
  w = 1;
  if (fW == 2,
    \\ residue of u in F_4^x made 1: w0 = u mod w (then u w0^2 = u^3 = 1 mod w)
    c = rich_lv_qres(LV, Qd, u); w = c[1] + c[2] * Mod(Qd[4] + Qd[5] * Qd[7], Qd[7]^2 - Qd[1]));
  for (it = 1, 2 * v2 + 2,
    t = rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, u * w^2 - 1); j = t[1];
    if (!t[2] || j >= 2 * v2 || j % 2, break);
    if (fW == 1, s = 1,
      c = rich_lv_qres(LV, Qd, (u * w^2 - 1) * rich_lv_pipow(LV, -j));
      s = (c[1] + c[2]) % 2 + c[2] * Mod(Qd[4] + Qd[5] * Qd[7], Qd[7]^2 - Qd[1]));
    w *= (1 + s * uni^(j / 2)));
  [if (eW == 1, rich_lv_pipow(LV, vz[1] / 2), if (vz[1] >= 0, uni^(vz[1] / 2), unii^(-vz[1] / 2))) * u * w, j];
}

\\ random points of R over K_v (Qd = 0) or quadratic points over the field Qd = K_v(sqrt eg), from the roots
\\ (rich_lv_roots) of f(x) - y0^2 (side model sd = 1) or f*(s) - y0^2 (sd = 2, x = 1/s). Fresh start (start = 0): x1
\\ random in O_v (resp. O_W) at a random depth and y0 an approximate square root of f(x1) (rich_lv_approxsqrt; for p
\\ odd or an odd valuation, y0 is random with v(y0) = floor(v(f(x1)) / 2)); when the approximation is good enough,
\\ Hensel's lemma puts a root near x1, whereas a random x gives a square f(x) with probability about
\\ 2^-([K_v : Q_2] + 1) only. Start near a known point, start = [sd, r, y], half of the time as a fresh start with
\\ x1 = r + pi^n u (n in [1, 2e]: the shallow levels), otherwise y0 = y + d with d = pi^k u, k = v(y) + a
\\ random shift in [0, 3e + 2], u a random unit (of O_W for a field); Hensel's lemma at r puts a root near r for k
\\ large, so the divisor (new point) - (known point) sweeps the formal group of the Jacobian at all levels.
\\ Returns a vector of [q, sd, r, y0]: r the local root (x or s), q the global point: an element x of K (Qd = 0; the
\\ caller checks it globally), or [al, be] with x = al + be sqrt(eg) not in K_v (reduced modulo Ib = pr^n; checked by
\\ rich_qcheck when kept)
rich_lv_ysample(LV, polys, Qd, eg, ntries, Ib, start = 0) =
{
  my(e = mapget(LV, "e"), E = mapget(LV, "E"), one = mapget(LV, "one"), out = List(), sd, m, x1, z, vz, ap, y0, rts, xx,
     toX, k, q, eW = if (Qd == 0, 1, Qd[3]));
  toX = ((a, b) -> if (Qd == 0, Mod(a, E) + one - 1,
                       Mod(Mod(a, E) + one - 1 + Mod(b, E) * Qd[4] + Mod(b, E) * Qd[5] * Qd[7], Qd[7]^2 - Qd[1])));
  for (it = 1, ntries,
    if (start != 0 && random(2),
      \\ near a known point: y0 = y + pi^k u
      sd = start[1];
      k = floor(rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, start[3])[1] / eW) + random(3 * e + 3);
      y0 = start[3] + rich_lv_pipow(LV, k) * toX(1 + rich_lY * rich_lv_rnd(LV, 0), if (Qd == 0, 0, rich_lv_rnd(LV, 0)))
    ,
      if (start != 0,
        \\ near a known point: x1 = r + pi^n u, n in [1, 2e] (the shallow levels, which y0 = y + d misses)
        sd = start[1];
        x1 = start[2] + rich_lv_pipow(LV, 1 + random(2 * e)) * toX(1 + rich_lY * rich_lv_rnd(LV, 0),
                                                                  if (Qd == 0, 0, rich_lv_rnd(LV, 0)))
      ,
        sd = 1 + random(2); m = if (random(2), 0, random(2 * e + 1));
        x1 = toX(rich_lv_rnd(LV, m), if (Qd == 0, 0, rich_lv_rnd(LV, m + if (random(2), 0, random(e + 1))))));
      z = subst(polys[sd][1], 'x, x1);
      ap = rich_lv_approxsqrt(LV, Qd, z);
      if (ap != 0, y0 = ap[1],
        vz = rich_lv_val(LV, if (Qd == 0, z, my(ab2 = rich_lv_ab(Qd, z)); ab2[1]^2 - Qd[1] * ab2[2]^2));
        if (!vz[2] || vz[1] == oo, next);
        k = floor(vz[1] / if (Qd == 0, 2, 4));
        y0 = rich_lv_pipow(LV, k) * toX(rich_lv_rnd(LV, 0), if (Qd == 0, 0, rich_lv_rnd(LV, 0)))));
    \\ y0 must not be too small: the global lift (modulo Ib) must keep the class of f(x) = y0^2
    if (rich_lv_vf(LV, Qd, y0)[1] > 10 * e * eW, next);
    rts = rich_lv_roots(LV, Qd, polys[sd][1] - y0^2);
    foreach (rts, r,
      if (Qd == 0,
        xx = rich_lv_lift(LV, r, Ib);
        if (sd == 2, if (xx == 0, next); xx = 1 / xx);
        listput(out, [xx, sd, r, y0])
      ,
        q = rich_lv_qglob(LV, Qd, eg, sd, r, Ib); if (q != 0, listput(out, [q, sd, r, y0])))));
  Vec(out);
}

\\ global quadratic point [al, be] (x = al + be sqrt(eg)) from a root r in M_W \ K_v of the side model sd (sd = 2:
\\ r is s = 1/x); al, be reduced modulo Ib; 0 when r lies in K_v (to precision)
rich_lv_qglob(LV, Qd, eg, sd, r, Ib) =
{
  my(ab = rich_lv_ab(Qd, r), vb, al, be, nn);
  vb = rich_lv_val(LV, ab[2]); if (!vb[2] || vb[1] == oo, return(0));
  al = rich_lv_lift(LV, ab[1], Ib); be = rich_lv_lift(LV, ab[2], Ib);
  if (be == 0, return(0));
  if (sd == 2, nn = al^2 - eg * be^2; if (nn == 0, return(0)); al = al / nn; be = -be / nn);
  [al, be];
}

\\ a random point of P^1(K_v) for the samplers: [sd, x0], x0 in pi^m O_v on the side model sd (x = x0 or x = 1/x0)
rich_lv_x0(LV) =
{
  my(m = if (random(2), 0, random(2 * mapget(LV, "e") + 1)));
  [1 + random(2), Mod(rich_lv_rnd(LV, m), mapget(LV, "E")) + mapget(LV, "one") - 1];
}

\\ one rational sample: [kappa value or 0, base value]; the point is x0 when given, else random
rich_try_rat(F, R, P, infr, base, x0 = []) =
{
  my(fx, g);
  if (x0 == [], x0 = rich_randx(F, P));
  fx = subst(mapget(R, "f"), 'x, x0);
  if (!rich_locsq(F, P, fx), return([0, base]));
  g = subst(mapget(R, "G2L"), 'x, rich_KtoL(F, x0));
  if (g == 0, return([0, base]));
  if (infr, return([g * mapget(R, "lcG2"), base]));
  if (base == 0, return([0, g]));
  [g * base, base];
}

\\ kappa value (global, in L) of the pair of conjugate points x = al + be sqrt(eg), pt = [al, be] (al, be, eg in K)
rich_qkappa(F, R, eg, pt) =
{
  my(u = x^2 - 2 * pt[1] * x + pt[1]^2 - eg * pt[2]^2);
  polresultant(rich_toLx(F, u), mapget(R, "G2L"), 'x);
}

\\ global check that f(x) is a nonzero square in M_W for x = al + be sqrt(eg) (Q = rich_quadfield(F, P, eg))
rich_qcheck(F, R, Q, pt) =
{
  my(x1 = rich_KtoM(F, Q, pt[1]) + rich_KtoM(F, Q, pt[2]) * Q[4], fx);
  fx = subst(Pol(apply(c -> rich_KtoM(F, Q, c), Vec(mapget(R, "f"))), 'x), 'x, x1);
  fx != 0 && rich_nfsq(Q[2], Q[5][1], fx);
}

\\ local images at P with the duality stopping rule. Finite places of degree one above p <= 3 use the local model
\\ (rich_lv_*): rational tree, then quadratic trees for the first rich_lv_qtrees fields (fields from rich_lv_fields:
\\ the classes of lc(f) and f(x0) first, then small representatives), then random rounds of y-sampling
\\ (rich_lv_ysample) on each side: fresh starts over K_v and over the fields in turn, fresh starts over the field of
\\ the class of f(x0) for a random x0 (new fields are added), and starts near points found earlier at a random scale.
\\ The rational points are checked globally by rich_try_rat and the quadratic points by rich_qcheck before they enter
\\ a basis. Other finite places: the same steps with the global trees (rich_ratpoints, rich_quadpoints,
\\ rich_try_quad) and random points. Real places: random rational points only.
rich_localimages(F, R, Rd, P, maxtries = 20000) =
{
  my(N = mapget(P, "N"), sides = [R, Rd], B = [[], []], V = [[], []], infr, base = [0, 0], t = 0, reps = [], QF,
     jq = 0, r, val, ntree = 0, fin = (mapget(P, "type") == 1), LV = 0, QL, polys, qpts = [List(), List()], pt, Ib,
     fidx = Map(), x0d, z0, c0, jn, near = [List(), List()], todo, nq, src = vector(6), nqbad = 0, jn2, done = 1, tstart = getabstime());
  if (N == 0, return([[], [], 0, [[], []], 0, 0, 1]));
  infr = [rich_infrat(F, R, P), rich_infrat(F, Rd, P)];
  if (fin, reps = rich_Kvclasses(F, P));
  if (fin && mapget(P, "pr").f == 1 && mapget(P, "p") <= 3,
    LV = rich_lv_init(F, P); polys = [rich_lv_curve(LV, R), rich_lv_curve(LV, Rd)];
    Ib = idealpow(mapget(F, "nfK"), mapget(P, "pr"), 40 * mapget(LV, "e"));
    reps = rich_lv_fields(F, sides, P, LV, reps));
  if (fin, QF = List(vector(#reps)); QL = List(vector(#reps)); reps = List(reps));
  if (LV != 0, for (j = 1, #reps, c0 = rich_lv_sqcoord(LV, rich_lv_map(LV, reps[j])); if (c0 != 0, mapput(fidx, c0, j))));
  \\ finite places: first the rational points from the residue disc tree
  if (fin,
    for (s = 1, 2,
      foreach (if (LV != 0, rich_lv_ratpoints(F, sides[s], P, LV), rich_ratpoints(F, sides[s], P)), x0,
        if (#B[1] + #B[2] >= N, break);
        r = rich_try_rat(F, sides[s], P, infr[s], base[s], x0); base[s] = r[2]; val = r[1];
        if (val != 0,
          r = rich_f2add(B[s], rich_loccoord(F, P, val));
          if (r[2], B[s] = r[1]; V[s] = concat(V[s], [val]))))));
  if (rich_verbose && fin, print("    [", mapget(P, "name"), "] rational trees: dims ", #B[1], " + ", #B[2], " of ", N,
                                 if (LV != 0, " (local model)", ""), ", ", #reps, " quadratic fields"));
  \\ then the quadratic points from the polydisc trees, field by field
  if (fin,
    for (jf = 1, if (LV != 0, min(rich_lv_qtrees, #reps), #reps),
      if (#B[1] + #B[2] >= N, break);
      if (rich_verbose && jf > 1, print("    [", mapget(P, "name"), "] after ", jf - 1, " fields: dims ", #B[1], " + ",
                                        #B[2], " of ", N));
      if (LV != 0,
        QL[jf] = rich_lv_quad(LV, rich_lv_map(LV, reps[jf]));
        for (s = 1, 2,
          foreach (rich_lv_quadpoints(F, sides[s], P, LV, QL[jf], reps[jf]), pt,
            if (#B[1] + #B[2] >= N, break);
            val = rich_qkappa(F, sides[s], reps[jf], pt);
            if (val == 0, next);
            r = rich_f2add(B[s], rich_loccoord(F, P, val));
            if (r[2], if (QF[jf] == 0, QF[jf] = rich_quadfield(F, P, reps[jf])); if (!rich_qcheck(F, sides[s], QF[jf], pt), nqbad++; r[2] = 0));
            if (r[2], B[s] = r[1]; V[s] = concat(V[s], [val]); listput(qpts[s], [jf, pt]))))
      ,
        if (QF[jf] == 0, QF[jf] = rich_quadfield(F, P, reps[jf]));
        for (s = 1, 2,
          foreach (rich_quadpoints(F, sides[s], P, QF[jf]), g,
            if (#B[1] + #B[2] >= N, break);
            r = rich_f2add(B[s], rich_loccoord(F, P, g));
            if (r[2], B[s] = r[1]; V[s] = concat(V[s], [g])))))));
  rich_chk(#B[1] + #B[2] <= N, Str("local duality violated at ", mapget(P, "name"), ": dims ", #B[1], " + ", #B[2],
                                   " > ", N));
  ntree = #B[1] + #B[2];
  while (#B[1] + #B[2] < N,
    t++;
    if (rich_verbose && t % 50 == 0, print("    [", mapget(P, "name"), "] random round ", t, ": dims ", #B[1], " + ", #B[2], " of ", N, if (LV != 0, Str(" (new from [fresh, native field, near] per side: ", src, "; ", #reps, " fields; ", nqbad, " quadratic points rejected by the global test; stack ", getstack() \ 10^6, " MB, heap ", getheap()[2] * 8 \ 10^6, " MB)"), ""), ", ", (getabstime() - tstart) \ 1000, " s"));
    if (rich_partial_ok && rich_time_budget > 0 && getabstime() - tstart > rich_time_budget, done = 0; break);
    if (t > maxtries,
      if (rich_partial_ok, done = 0; break);
      error("richelot: local image sampling incomplete at ", mapget(P, "name"), ": dims ", #B[1], " + ", #B[2],
            " < ", N));
    if (LV != 0,
      \\ local model, each side: y-sampling (rich_lv_ysample) from (a) a fresh start over K_v (jq = 0) or over the
      \\ cycled field jq, (b) a fresh start over the field of the class of f(x0) for a random x0 (added to the list
      \\ when new; for a curve without K_v-points these are the fields that carry points), (c) a start near a point
      \\ found earlier, at a random scale (differences of nearby points fill the formal group part of the image)
      jq = (jq + 1) % (#reps + 1);
      if (jq > 0 && QL[jq] == 0, QL[jq] = rich_lv_quad(LV, rich_lv_map(LV, reps[jq])));
      for (s = 1, 2,
        x0d = rich_lv_x0(LV); z0 = subst(polys[s][x0d[1]][1], 'x, x0d[2]); c0 = rich_lv_sqcoord(LV, z0); jn = 0;
        if (c0 != 0 && c0 != vector(#c0),
          if (!mapisdefined(fidx, c0, &jn),
            listput(reps, rich_lv_classrep(LV, z0)); listput(QF, 0); listput(QL, 0); jn = #reps; mapput(fidx, c0, jn));
          if (QL[jn] == 0, QL[jn] = rich_lv_quad(LV, rich_lv_map(LV, reps[jn]))));
        todo = [[jq, 0], [jn, 0]];
        if (#near[s],
          nq = near[s][1 + random(#near[s])];
          \\ near a rational point, half of the time into a random field: quadratic points P + P' near 2 P0 give
          \\ both directions of the formal group at every level
          jn2 = nq[1];
          if (jn2 == 0 && random(2), jn2 = 1 + random(#reps); if (QL[jn2] == 0, QL[jn2] = rich_lv_quad(LV, rich_lv_map(LV, reps[jn2]))));
          todo = concat(todo, [[jn2, [nq[2], nq[3], nq[4]]]]));
        for (kk = 1, #todo, my(td = todo[kk]);
          foreach (rich_lv_ysample(LV, polys[s], if (td[1] == 0, 0, QL[td[1]]), if (td[1] == 0, 0, reps[td[1]]), 1, Ib,
                                   td[2]), pt,
            if (#near[s] < 400, listput(near[s], [td[1], pt[2], pt[3], pt[4]]), near[s][1 + random(400)] = [td[1], pt[2], pt[3], pt[4]]);
            if (td[1] == 0,
              r = rich_try_rat(F, sides[s], P, infr[s], base[s], pt[1]); base[s] = r[2]; val = r[1]
            ,
              val = rich_qkappa(F, sides[s], reps[td[1]], pt[1]));
            if (val != 0,
              r = rich_f2add(B[s], rich_loccoord(F, P, val));
              if (r[2] && td[1] > 0, if (QF[td[1]] == 0, QF[td[1]] = rich_quadfield(F, P, reps[td[1]]));
                if (!rich_qcheck(F, sides[s], QF[td[1]], pt[1]), nqbad++; r[2] = 0));
              if (r[2], B[s] = r[1]; V[s] = concat(V[s], [val]); src[3 * (s - 1) + kk]++; if (td[1] > 0, listput(qpts[s], [td[1], pt[1]])))))))
    ,
      if (fin, jq = jq % #reps + 1; if (QF[jq] == 0, QF[jq] = rich_quadfield(F, P, reps[jq])));
      for (s = 1, 2,
        r = rich_try_rat(F, sides[s], P, infr[s], base[s]); base[s] = r[2];
        val = [r[1]];
        if (fin, val = concat(val, [rich_try_quad(F, sides[s], P, QF[jq])]));
        for (i = 1, #val,
          if (val[i] != 0,
            r = rich_f2add(B[s], rich_loccoord(F, P, val[i]));
            if (r[2], B[s] = r[1]; V[s] = concat(V[s], [val[i]]))))));
    rich_chk(#B[1] + #B[2] <= N, Str("local duality violated at ", mapget(P, "name"), ": dims ", #B[1], " + ",
                                     #B[2], " > ", N)));
  \\ assertion: the quadratic points of the local model kept in the bases passed rich_qcheck when they entered
  for (s = 1, 2, foreach (qpts[s], q,
    if (QF[q[1]] == 0, QF[q[1]] = rich_quadfield(F, P, reps[q[1]]));
    rich_chk(rich_qcheck(F, sides[s], QF[q[1]], q[2]), Str("local model: a quadratic point fails the global test at ",
                                                            mapget(P, "name")))));
  [B[1], B[2], N, V, t, ntree, done];
}

\\ Hilbert symbol pairing matrices between the sampled bases (diagnostic): [pairing (a,b), pairing (a, tau b)],
\\ each an F2 matrix; local Tate duality predicts that one of the two natural pairings vanishes identically
rich_pairings(F, P, V1, V2) =
{
  my(nfL = mapget(F, "nfL"), M0, M1);
  M0 = matrix(#V1, #V2, i, j, rich_hpair(nfL, P, V1[i], V2[j]));
  M1 = matrix(#V1, #V2, i, j, rich_hpair(nfL, P, V1[i], rich_tau(F, V2[j])));
  [M0, M1];
}

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- S, L(S,2), Selmer groups
\\ rational primes below every prime of K where the model of F is not smooth or not integral: 2, the norms of the
\\ discriminant and of the leading coefficient, the denominators of the coefficients (a superset of the bad primes of J)
rich_badprimes(F, R) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), f = mapget(R, "f"), N = 2, nm);
  nm = (a -> if (type(a) == "t_POLMOD", norm(a), a));
  N *= abs(numerator(nm(poldisc(f)))) * abs(denominator(nm(poldisc(f))));
  N *= abs(numerator(nm(pollead(f))));
  foreach (rich_xcoefs(f), c, if (c != 0, N *= denominator(nfalgtobasis(nfK, c))));
  Vec(factor(N)[, 1]);
}

\\ class of the ideal W in Cl(L) / 2, restricted to the even cyclic factors ev
rich_clvec(bnf, ev, W) = { my(c = bnfisprincipal(bnf, W, 0)); vector(#ev, i, c[ev[i]] % 2)~; }

\\ valuation of an element or famat at a prime
rich_val(nf, a, pr) =
{
  if (type(a) == "t_MAT", return(sum(i = 1, #a~, a[i, 2] * rich_val(nf, a[i, 1], pr))));
  nfeltval(nf, rich_alg(nf, a), pr);
}

rich_places(F, R, badp) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), Kpol = mapget(F, "Kpol"), ps = Set(concat([2], badp)), prs = List(), rd, fa, pl = List());
  foreach (ps, p, foreach (idealprimedec(nfK, p), pr, listput(prs, pr)));
  \\ rnfdisc needs an integral polynomial: d times the square of its denominator (same field L)
  my(dd = mapget(F, "d"), dl);
  dl = if (type(dd) == "t_POLMOD", lift(dd), dd); dl *= denominator(content(dl))^2;
  rd = rnfdisc(nfK, x^2 - dl);
  fa = idealfactor(nfK, rd[1]);
  for (i = 1, #fa~, if (!setsearch(ps, fa[i, 1].p),
    warning("richelot: L/K ramifies at a prime above ", fa[i, 1].p, " not in the bad list: added");
    listput(prs, fa[i, 1])));
  foreach (prs, pr, listput(pl, rich_place(F, pr)));
  foreach (mapget(F, "real"), r, listput(pl, rich_place(F, r[1])));
  Vec(pl);
}

rich_LS2(F, SL) =
{
  my(bnf = mapget(F, "bnfL"), cyc = bnf.cyc, ev, cl, M, A = List(), Sp = Set([w.p | w <- SL]), U, r);
  rich_chk(type(bnf) == "t_VEC", "rich_LS2 needs rich_fields(..., wantbnf = 1)");
  ev = [i | i <- [1..#cyc], cyc[i] % 2 == 0];
  M = vector(#SL, j, rich_clvec(bnf, ev, SL[j]));
  r = if (#SL == 0 || #ev == 0, 0, matrank(Mod(Mat(M), 2)));
  forprime (q = 2, oo,
    if (r == #ev, break);
    if (setsearch(Sp, q), next);
    foreach (idealprimedec(bnf, q), W,
      if (r < #ev && matrank(Mod(Mat(concat(M, [rich_clvec(bnf, ev, W)])), 2)) > r, M = concat(M, [rich_clvec(bnf, ev, W)]); listput(A, W); r++)));
  U = bnfunits(bnf, concat(SL, Vec(A)));
  [U[1], Vec(A)];
}

rich_tors2(F, R) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), f = mapget(R, "f"), fa, nl = 0, nq = 0, cnt, t);
  fa = if (poldegree(nfK.pol) == 1, factor(f), nffactor(nfK, f));
  for (i = 1, #fa~,
    rich_chk(fa[i, 2] == 1, "f not squarefree");
    if (poldegree(fa[i, 1], 'x) == 1, nl++);
    if (poldegree(fa[i, 1], 'x) == 2, nq++));
  if (poldegree(f, 'x) == 5, nl++);
  cnt = 1 + nq + nl * (nl - 1) / 2;
  t = valuation(cnt, 2);
  rich_chk(cnt == 2^t, Str("#J(K)[2] = ", cnt, " is not a power of 2"));
  t;
}

\\ Gram matrices [G1, G0] of the pairings (a, b) -> sum_w (a, tau b)_w and (a, b) -> sum_w (a, b)_w on L_v^x / L_v^x2
\\ (w over the primes or real places of L above P) in the coordinates of rich_loccoord: the pairing of a and b is
\\ c(a)~ * G * c(b) mod 2. Built from random small elements E_i of L whose coordinates span F2^N. Both pairings are
\\ symmetric (tau permutes the w), so only the N (N + 1) / 2 Hilbert symbols h(E_i, tau E_j), i <= j, are computed;
\\ G0 = G1 * T with T the matrix of tau on the coordinates. G1 is checked to be invertible (the Hilbert pairing is
\\ perfect). Above 2 a Hilbert symbol costs seconds in large degree (nfhilbert): N = 26 in degree 42 takes minutes.
rich_gram(F, P) =
{
  my(nfL = mapget(F, "nfL"), N = mapget(P, "N"), E = [], C = [], e, c, n = poldegree(nfL.pol), M, Ci, G, T, cnt = 0,
     U = [], W, Et);
  if (N == 0, return([matrix(0, 0), matrix(0, 0)]));
  \\ U: for each prime w of L above P an element of valuation 1 at w and 0 at the other primes above P
  if (mapget(P, "type") == 1, W = mapget(P, "W");
    U = vector(#W, i, rich_alg(nfL, idealappr(nfL, matrix(#W, 2, j, c2, if (c2 == 1, W[j], j == i))))));
  while (#E < N,
    cnt++; rich_chk(cnt <= 200 * N, Str("rich_gram: random coordinates do not span at ", mapget(P, "name")));
    e = nfbasistoalg(nfL, vectorv(n, i, random(9) - 4));
    if (e == 0, next);
    \\ small elements are units at a prime of large norm: multiply by uniformizers at random
    for (i = 1, #U, if (random(2), e *= U[i]));
    c = rich_loccoord(F, P, e);
    if (matrank(Mod(Mat(concat(C, [c])), 2)) > #C, C = concat(C, [c]); E = concat(E, [e])));
  Et = apply(a -> rich_tau(F, a), E);
  M = matrix(N, N);
  for (i = 1, N, for (j = i, N, M[i, j] = rich_hpair(nfL, P, E[i], Et[j]); M[j, i] = M[i, j]));
  Ci = Mod(Mat(C), 2)^(-1);
  G = lift(Ci~ * Mod(M, 2) * Ci);
  rich_chk(matrank(Mod(G, 2)) == N, Str("rich_gram: degenerate pairing at ", mapget(P, "name")));
  T = lift(Mod(Mat(vector(N, j, rich_loccoord(F, P, Et[j]))), 2) * Ci);
  [G, (G * T) % 2];
}

rich_colmat(B, N) = if (#B == 0, matrix(N, 0), Mat(B));

\\ Selmer bounds from local images that may be partial (loc[k] from rich_localimages with rich_partial_ok = 1, for the
\\ places pl = rich_places(F, R, badp)). Returns a Map:
\\   "low" [dim, dim']: the subgroup of L(S,2) whose localizations lie in the spans of the sampled bases; it is
\\       contained in the Selmer group without any hypothesis (the sampled classes are local images);
\\   "up" [dim, dim']: localizations orthogonal, for the pairing sum_w (a, tau b)_w, to the sampled basis of the other
\\       side; Im kappa_v and Im kappa'_v are exact annihilators under the local Tate pairing, so this contains the
\\       Selmer group once the Tate pairing is identified with the tau pairing (see "tw");
\\   at a complete place (dims adding up to N) both bounds use the exact image, so low = up when every place is complete;
\\   "tw": [number of complete places where the tau pairing vanishes on the images and the plain pairing does not,
\\       number of places (complete or not) where the tau pairing fails to vanish on the sampled bases]. The Galois
\\       invariant perfect pairings on Res_{L/K} mu_2 are the plain one and the tau one, so a count [>= 1, 0] fixes
\\       the identification; with [0, 0] the upper bound is conditional on it;
\\   "T0": kappa(T0) and kappa'(T0') satisfy the upper bound conditions at every place (consistency);
\\   "LS2dim", "locrank": dimension of the computed L(S,2) and rank of its localization at the places in pl (equal
\\       means the generators are independent modulo squares, a check that needs no GRH);
\\   "places": per place [name, N, #basis, #basis', complete, tau pairing vanishes, plain pairing vanishes] (-1: not
\\       computed, N > gramN; such a place gives no upper bound condition unless it is complete);
\\   "cassels" [lo, hi]: bounds for dim Sel^phihat - dim Sel^phi from the Greenberg-Wiles formula (see the header);
\\   "low0", "up0": the bounds before the Cassels refinement; "low", "up" are refined by it (the refined lower bound
\\       uses the formula, a theorem, and still needs neither GRH nor the pairing identification);
\\   "consistent": low <= up on both sides (a failure would reveal an error).
rich_selmer_bounds(F, R, Rd, pl, loc, gramN = oo) =
{
  my(out = Map(), nfL = mapget(F, "nfL"), SL = List(), LS, gens, A, n, C, G = vector(#pl), G0, cB, low = [0, 0],
     up = [0, 0], rowsL, rowsU, twc = 0, twbad = 0, info = List(), c1, c2, z1, z0, N, comp, crank, T0, okT0 = 1, r, cc,
     nfK, c0, clo, chi, tv, low0, up0);
  foreach (pl, P, if (mapget(P, "type") == 1, foreach (mapget(P, "W"), w, listput(SL, w))));
  LS = rich_LS2(F, Vec(SL)); gens = LS[1]; A = LS[2]; n = #gens;
  rich_chk(matrix(#A, n, i, j, rich_val(nfL, gens[j], A[i]) % 2) == 0, "odd valuation at an auxiliary prime");
  C = vector(#pl, k, if (loc[k][3] == 0, matrix(0, n), rich_loccoords(F, pl[k], gens)));
  crank = matrank(Mod(matconcat(concat([matrix(0, n)], Vec(C))~), 2));
  for (k = 1, #pl, N = loc[k][3]; if (N > 0,
    comp = (#loc[k][1] + #loc[k][2] == N); z1 = -1; z0 = -1;
    if (N <= gramN,
      my(GG = rich_gram(F, pl[k])); G[k] = GG[1]; G0 = GG[2];
      c1 = rich_colmat(loc[k][1], N); c2 = rich_colmat(loc[k][2], N);
      if (#loc[k][1] == 0 || #loc[k][2] == 0, z1 = 1; z0 = 1, z1 = (c1~ * G[k] * c2) % 2 == 0; z0 = (c1~ * G0 * c2) % 2 == 0);
      if (!z1, twbad++);
      if (comp && z1 && !z0, twc++));
    listput(info, [mapget(pl[k], "name"), N, #loc[k][1], #loc[k][2], comp, z1, z0])));
  T0 = [rich_kappa(F, R, mapget(R, "G1")), rich_kappa(F, Rd, mapget(Rd, "G1"))];
  for (s = 1, 2,
    rowsL = matrix(0, n); rowsU = matrix(0, n);
    for (k = 1, #pl, N = loc[k][3]; if (N > 0,
      r = rich_annih(loc[k][s], N);
      rowsL = matconcat([rowsL; r * C[k]]);
      if (#loc[k][1] + #loc[k][2] < N,
        cB = rich_colmat(loc[k][3 - s], N);
        \\ side 1: h(x, tau b) = c(x)~ G c(b) = 0 for b in Im kappa'_v; side 2: h(a, tau x) = c(a)~ G c(x) = 0
        r = if (#loc[k][3 - s] == 0 || type(G[k]) != "t_MAT", matrix(0, N), if (s == 1, cB~ * G[k]~, cB~ * G[k]) % 2));
      rowsU = matconcat([rowsU; r * C[k]]);
      cc = rich_loccoord(F, pl[k], T0[s]);
      if ((r * cc) % 2 != 0, okT0 = 0)));
    low[s] = n - matrank(Mod(rowsL, 2)); up[s] = n - matrank(Mod(rowsU, 2)));
  \\ Greenberg-Wiles (Cassels) formula: dim Sel - dim Sel' = sum over all places v of (dim Im kappa_v - t_v) with
  \\ t_v = dim H^0(K_v, J'[phihat]) (the global terms cancel: T0 and T0' are the only nonzero rational points of the
  \\ kernels). A place outside pl not above 2 contributes 0 (unramified classes), a complex place -2, a real place of K
  \\ not split in L -1, a place of pl dim Im kappa_v - t_v with t_v = 1 + [v splits in L]. The sampled bases bound
  \\ dim Im kappa_v between #basis and N - #basis'; this needs neither GRH nor the tau identification.
  nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"); c0 = -2 * nfK.sign[2] - (nfK.sign[1] - #mapget(F, "real")); clo = c0; chi = c0;
  for (k = 1, #pl, N = loc[k][3];
    tv = 1 + (mapget(pl[k], "type") == 0 || #mapget(pl[k], "W") == 2);
    clo += #loc[k][1] - tv; chi += N - #loc[k][2] - tv);
  low0 = low; up0 = up;
  for (it = 1, 4,
    low[1] = max(low[1], low[2] + clo); up[1] = min(up[1], up[2] + chi);
    low[2] = max(low[2], low[1] - chi); up[2] = min(up[2], up[1] - clo));
  mapput(out, "cassels", [clo, chi]); mapput(out, "low0", low0); mapput(out, "up0", up0);
  mapput(out, "consistent", low[1] <= up[1] && low[2] <= up[2]);
  mapput(out, "low", low); mapput(out, "up", up); mapput(out, "tw", [twc, twbad]); mapput(out, "T0", okT0);
  mapput(out, "LS2dim", n); mapput(out, "locrank", crank); mapput(out, "aux", #A); mapput(out, "places", Vec(info));
  mapput(out, "gens", gens);
  out;
}

\\ Selmer groups of the Richelot isogeny pair and the rank bound
rich_selmer(F, R, Rd, badp, verbose = 0) =
{
  my(out = Map(), pl, loc = List(), SL = List(), LS, gens, A, n, C, rows, valA, sel = [0, 0], selv = [0, 0], nfL,
     li, cond, T0, T0d, t2, t2d, info = List(), K2);
  nfL = mapget(F, "nfL");
  pl = rich_places(F, R, badp);
  foreach (pl, P,
    li = rich_localimages(F, R, Rd, P);
    listput(loc, li);
    \\ info: [place, dim H^1, dim Im(kappa), dim Im(kappa'), [pairing (a, b) vanishes on the images, pairing
    \\ (a, tau b) vanishes]]; exactly one of the two is the Tate pairing, which must vanish at every place
    my(pm = if (li[3] > 0, rich_pairings(F, P, li[4][1], li[4][2]), [[;], [;]]));
    listput(info, [mapget(P, "name"), li[3], #li[1], #li[2], [pm[1] == 0, pm[2] == 0]]);
    if (verbose, print("  local ", mapget(P, "name"), ": dim H^1 = ", li[3], ", Im(kappa) ", #li[1], ", Im(kappa') ", #li[2]));
    if (mapget(P, "type") == 1, foreach (mapget(P, "W"), w, listput(SL, w))));
  LS = rich_LS2(F, Vec(SL)); gens = LS[1]; A = LS[2]; n = #gens;
  \\ every S u A unit must have even valuation at the auxiliary primes
  valA = matrix(#A, n, i, j, rich_val(nfL, gens[j], A[i]) % 2);
  rich_chk(valA == 0, "odd valuation at an auxiliary prime");
  C = vector(#pl, k, if (loc[k][3] == 0, matrix(0, n), rich_loccoords(F, pl[k], gens)));
  for (s = 1, 2,
    rows = matrix(0, n);
    for (k = 1, #pl, if (loc[k][3] > 0, rows = matconcat([rows; rich_annih(loc[k][s], loc[k][3]) * C[k]])));
    K2 = if (matsize(rows)[1] == 0, matid(n), lift(matker(Mod(rows, 2))));
    selv[s] = K2; sel[s] = matsize(K2)[2]);
  \\ torsion and consistency checks: kappa(T0) in Sel^phihat, kappa'(T0') in Sel^phi
  T0 = rich_kappa(F, R, mapget(R, "G1")); T0d = rich_kappa(F, Rd, mapget(Rd, "G1"));
  for (k = 1, #pl, if (loc[k][3] > 0,
    rich_chk(#rich_f2add(loc[k][1], rich_loccoord(F, pl[k], T0))[1] == #loc[k][1], "kappa(T0) not in the local image");
    rich_chk(#rich_f2add(loc[k][2], rich_loccoord(F, pl[k], T0d))[1] == #loc[k][2], "kappa'(T0') not in the local image")));
  t2 = rich_tors2(F, R); t2d = rich_tors2(F, Rd);
  mapput(out, "shat", sel[1]); mapput(out, "s", sel[2]); mapput(out, "bound", sel[1] + sel[2] - 2);
  mapput(out, "selhat", selv[1]); mapput(out, "sel", selv[2]); mapput(out, "gens", gens);
  mapput(out, "t2", t2); mapput(out, "t2d", t2d); mapput(out, "LS2dim", n); mapput(out, "aux", #A);
  mapput(out, "local", Vec(info)); mapput(out, "grh", 1); mapput(out, "places", pl); mapput(out, "loc", Vec(loc));
  out;
}

\\ ---------------------------------------------------------------- reduction modulo a degree one prime (tests)
rich_reduce(F, R, pr) =
{
  my(nfK = mapget(F, "nfK"), p = pr.p, mp = 0, rx);
  rich_chk(pr.f == 1, "rich_reduce needs a degree one prime");
  if (poldegree(nfK.pol) > 1, mp = nfmodprinit(nfK, pr));
  rx = [vector(3, j, rich_redp(F, nfK, p, mp, polcoef(mapget(R, k), j - 1, 'x))) | k <- ["G1", "A", "B"]];
  [p, rich_redp(F, nfK, p, mp, mapget(F, "d")), rich_redp(F, nfK, p, mp, mapget(R, "c")), rx[1], rx[2], rx[3]];
}
